00:01:22.161 --> 00:01:24.030
<i>So, I know
what you're thinking.</i>


00:01:24.163 --> 00:01:26.432
<i>Why is that incredibly
handsome hedgehog</i>


00:01:26.565 --> 00:01:27.766
<i>being chased by a madman</i>


00:01:27.899 --> 00:01:29.835
<i>with a mustache
from the Civil War?</i>


00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:33.905
<i>Well, to be honest, it feels like
I've been running my whole life.</i>


00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.342
<i>Is this too much?
Am I going too fast?</i>


00:01:36.476 --> 00:01:39.479
<i>It's kind of what I do...
You know what? Let's back up.</i>


00:01:47.186 --> 00:01:50.189
<i>This is the island
where I'm from.</i>


00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:52.225
<i>It had everything.</i>


00:01:52.358 --> 00:01:54.760
<i>Sandy beaches,
cascading waterfalls,</i>


00:01:54.893 --> 00:01:56.728
<i>public access to loop-de-loops.</i>


00:01:56.862 --> 00:01:58.663
<i>And, I never had
to catch a school bus</i>


00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:01.134
<i>because I could run across
the entire island</i>


00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.834
<i>in less than two seconds.</i>


00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:04.703
<i>Also, there was no school.</i>


00:02:04.836 --> 00:02:07.173
<i>I know,
pretty sweet island, right?</i>


00:02:08.007 --> 00:02:09.008
Yeah!


00:02:09.142 --> 00:02:11.044
<i>I was born
with extraordinary powers</i>


00:02:11.177 --> 00:02:12.778
<i>and was told
to keep them secret.</i>


00:02:12.911 --> 00:02:15.547
<i>And like any kid,
I did the exact opposite.</i>


00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.983
Whoo-hoo!


00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:20.819
<i>That's Longclaw.
She took care of me.</i>


00:02:20.953 --> 00:02:22.989
<i>She was basically
Obi-Wan Kenobi...</i>


00:02:23.122 --> 00:02:25.458
<i>if Obi-Wan Kenobi
had a beak and ate mice.</i>


00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.161
Sonic, someone
could have seen you.


00:02:28.294 --> 00:02:30.762
No one saw me. I'm too fast!


00:02:30.896 --> 00:02:32.965
And I wanted to bring you this.


00:02:36.768 --> 00:02:38.204
Get down!


00:02:41.673 --> 00:02:43.042
<i>Turns out,
with great power</i>


00:02:43.176 --> 00:02:45.278
<i>comes great
power-hungry bad guys.</i>


00:02:45.411 --> 00:02:47.646
<i>And I led them right to us.</i>


00:03:02.261 --> 00:03:04.663
Listen carefully, Sonic.


00:03:04.796 --> 00:03:07.699
You have a power unlike
anything I have ever seen.


00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:10.036
And that means someone
will always want it.


00:03:10.169 --> 00:03:14.173
The only way to stay safe
is to stay hidden.


00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.246
This world is on the far side
of the universe.


00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:21.547
You should be safe there.


00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.217
- I don't want to go without you.
- You must.


00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.953
These rings will be your most
important possession.


00:03:30.889 --> 00:03:33.493
If you're ever discovered,
use one.


00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:36.162
Never stop running.


00:03:36.661 --> 00:03:38.197
Now go!


00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.169
Longclaw!


00:03:44.636 --> 00:03:45.605
Goodbye, Sonic.


00:03:45.737 --> 00:03:46.771
No!


00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:50.775
No!


00:04:16.536 --> 00:04:18.137
Come on, one car?


00:04:28.281 --> 00:04:29.282
I'm bored.


00:04:29.415 --> 00:04:31.716
<i>Tom, do you read me?
Are you there?</i>


00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.154
No, Wade, I'm actually
on a yacht in Barbados.


00:04:35.921 --> 00:04:37.256
With Rihanna.


00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.723
OMG.


00:04:38.857 --> 00:04:40.459
That's amazing.
Please send pics.


00:04:40.593 --> 00:04:42.361
No, Wade.
I'm at the speed trap.


00:04:42.495 --> 00:04:45.764
Already? How did you get back so fast?
Barbados is in the ocean!


00:04:45.897 --> 00:04:47.934
Hang on, I think
I got something.


00:04:54.839 --> 00:04:57.809
Hey, buddy! Where's the fire?


00:04:57.944 --> 00:04:59.946
Got kids living around here.


00:05:00.812 --> 00:05:01.846
I thought that was
kind of funny.


00:05:01.981 --> 00:05:03.482
Sorry.


00:05:09.488 --> 00:05:10.990
What?


00:05:49.629 --> 00:05:51.497
<i>Tom,
we need you down on Main Street.</i>


00:05:51.631 --> 00:05:53.633
<i>There's been a violent
gang shoot-out.</i>


00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:58.471
<i>Just kidding.
A duck stole a bagel.</i>


00:05:58.604 --> 00:06:00.905
<i>But they do need it back.</i>


00:06:11.384 --> 00:06:14.287
Whoa, buddy, you almost
got yourself killed out there.


00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.389
What are you,
some kind of adrenaline junkie?


00:06:16.522 --> 00:06:18.724
It must be rough
being slow all the time.


00:06:18.857 --> 00:06:22.028
Tell you what.
Today is your lucky day.


00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.532
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!


00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:29.168
Have you ever felt so alive?


00:06:30.269 --> 00:06:32.804
This is great.
You're doing amazing.


00:06:32.938 --> 00:06:34.540
Oh, geez!


00:06:34.974 --> 00:06:36.875
Good recovery.


00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:39.211
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!


00:06:39.345 --> 00:06:41.813
Let's keep this our little secret, okay?


00:06:41.947 --> 00:06:45.017
You never saw me.
I was never here.


00:06:59.365 --> 00:07:01.067
<i>So what
were you expecting?</i>


00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.069
<i>A dirty little hedgehog
eating berries</i>


00:07:03.202 --> 00:07:05.204
<i>and struggling to survive?</i>


00:07:05.338 --> 00:07:09.809
<i>Think again. Because I am
living my best life on Earth.</i>


00:07:09.942 --> 00:07:11.910
<i>I've got a library...</i>


00:07:13.112 --> 00:07:14.580
<i>a home gym,</i>


00:07:14.714 --> 00:07:17.516
<i>and a state-of-the-art
security system.</i>


00:07:29.762 --> 00:07:30.996
Oh, no.


00:07:32.098 --> 00:07:33.332
<i>And, if I'm ever discovered,</i>


00:07:33.466 --> 00:07:35.067
<i>I'll follow
Longclaw's instructions</i>


00:07:35.201 --> 00:07:38.371
<i>and use my rings
to escape to a new planet.</i>


00:07:38.504 --> 00:07:42.641
<i>A nice, safe little world
filled only with mushrooms.</i>


00:07:43.943 --> 00:07:47.113
<i>Gross, smelly mushrooms.</i>


00:07:47.847 --> 00:07:49.615
I hate mushrooms.


00:07:50.683 --> 00:07:52.884
<i>But let's not worry
about all that.</i>


00:07:53.018 --> 00:07:55.254
<i>This is Green Hills.</i>


00:07:55.388 --> 00:07:57.590
<i>The greatest place on Earth.</i>


00:07:58.858 --> 00:08:01.127
<i>These are my people and,
dare I say,</i>


00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.529
<i>I am their
lovable space creature.</i>


00:08:03.662 --> 00:08:06.399
<i>So what if they
don't know I exist?</i>


00:08:07.533 --> 00:08:11.103
<i>My favorite person
is the Donut Lord.</i>


00:08:11.804 --> 00:08:13.939
<i>Protector of this town</i>


00:08:14.073 --> 00:08:17.209
<i>and defender of all creatures,
big and small.</i>


00:08:17.343 --> 00:08:18.110
Morning.


00:08:18.244 --> 00:08:20.246
Donald. Daisy. Daffy.


00:08:21.213 --> 00:08:24.183
<i>Donut Lord lives
with Pretzel Lady.</i>


00:08:24.316 --> 00:08:25.917
<i>She is super nice to animals</i>


00:08:26.051 --> 00:08:29.555
<i>and strangely was born
without bones.</i>


00:08:29.688 --> 00:08:31.023
Ouch, ouch, ouch.


00:08:31.157 --> 00:08:32.858
<i>There is one person in town</i>


00:08:32.992 --> 00:08:34.260
<i>who's actually onto me.</i>


00:08:34.393 --> 00:08:36.695
<i>He calls me the blue devil.</i>


00:08:36.829 --> 00:08:38.664
I almost caught him last night.


00:08:38.798 --> 00:08:40.599
<i>Say hello to Crazy Carl.</i>


00:08:44.203 --> 00:08:45.971
<i>We have fun together.</i>


00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:49.875
I know you're out there!


00:08:50.009 --> 00:08:52.878
And I know you're real!


00:08:53.012 --> 00:08:55.581
No, I'm not!


00:08:55.714 --> 00:08:57.516
<i>Movie night is my favorite.</i>


00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.319
Please, please,
please, please, please.


00:09:00.453 --> 00:09:01.754
Yes! Keanu!


00:09:01.887 --> 00:09:03.322
You are a national treasure.


00:09:03.456 --> 00:09:05.891
- <i>When I find you...</i>
- <i>Pop quiz, hotshot.</i>


00:09:06.025 --> 00:09:07.760
<i>There's a bomb on a bus.</i>


00:09:07.893 --> 00:09:09.728
"Pop quiz, hotshot."


00:09:09.862 --> 00:09:11.430
It's a classic line.


00:09:11.564 --> 00:09:14.166
<i>Basically,
we're like a family.</i>


00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.068
<i>Even though we haven't met yet.</i>


00:09:16.202 --> 00:09:18.070
You don't zink your


00:09:18.204 --> 00:09:20.739
prolonged isolation is making
you a bit crazy perhaps?


00:09:20.873 --> 00:09:22.741
Crazy? Me?


00:09:22.875 --> 00:09:25.311
No way, Doc.
You got me all wrong.


00:09:25.444 --> 00:09:29.648
And despite all these so-called
friends of yours, deep down...


00:09:29.782 --> 00:09:32.251
...you're still rather lonely?


00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.260
<i>Perhaps afraid
you'll be alone forever?</i>


00:09:55.241 --> 00:09:58.979
Uh-uh. Hey!
No, no, no, no.


00:09:59.111 --> 00:10:00.746
Get out of there. Come on.


00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.082
Oh, come on! Get out of there!


00:10:03.215 --> 00:10:05.784
Get out of there,
you trash pandas.


00:10:07.286 --> 00:10:09.788
Maddie, as Green Hills'
most respected veterinarian,


00:10:09.922 --> 00:10:13.092
what is the fastest way
to exterminate a raccoon?


00:10:13.225 --> 00:10:15.728
Hi, Ozzy. Hello!
You're glad to see me.


00:10:15.861 --> 00:10:17.229
You don't eat garbage, do you?


00:10:17.998 --> 00:10:19.532
What's that?


00:10:19.665 --> 00:10:23.102
- Is that what I think it is?
- Uh-huh. Open it.


00:10:23.235 --> 00:10:25.037
Oh, it's kind of small.
Is that bad?


00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.172
Just open it.


00:10:32.111 --> 00:10:33.479
"Dear Thomas:


00:10:33.612 --> 00:10:34.948
We have reviewed
your application


00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.415
to the San Francisco
Police Department,


00:10:36.549 --> 00:10:38.150
and pending
interdepartmental review


00:10:38.284 --> 00:10:40.386
and background check,
we are happy to inform you


00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:42.421
that you have been selected
to join our team."


00:10:42.555 --> 00:10:44.490
- Oh, my God!
- Wow.


00:10:44.958 --> 00:10:46.458
Oh, my God.


00:10:46.825 --> 00:10:48.060
Ta-da!


00:10:48.761 --> 00:10:50.696
"San Francisco Sucks."


00:10:50.829 --> 00:10:52.598
Oh!


00:10:52.731 --> 00:10:53.766
Wrong one!


00:10:55.936 --> 00:10:57.903
Ta-da!


00:10:58.704 --> 00:11:01.774
- You never had a doubt, huh?
- No! Mm-mmm.


00:11:03.842 --> 00:11:07.346
- I can't believe this.
- Oh, I know! You did it.


00:11:08.881 --> 00:11:10.449
Hey, what are those?


00:11:11.417 --> 00:11:13.652
Apartments for rent
I found on Zillow.


00:11:13.786 --> 00:11:16.255
I thought Ozzy and I
could fly there tomorrow


00:11:16.388 --> 00:11:19.391
and check out
some neighborhoods.


00:11:19.525 --> 00:11:22.261
I mean,
this is all happening so fast.


00:11:22.394 --> 00:11:25.065
Oh, man...
It's the craziest thing.


00:11:25.197 --> 00:11:27.333
You apply for the job,
you get the job.


00:11:27.466 --> 00:11:29.002
Well, pending
a background check.


00:11:29.134 --> 00:11:31.071
Oh, man.
Hope they don't find out about


00:11:31.203 --> 00:11:33.539
that time you used
the neighbor's Wi-Fi.


00:11:33.672 --> 00:11:35.774
Correction: I'm still using
the neighbor's Wi-Fi.


00:11:35.908 --> 00:11:38.143
But, Maddie,


00:11:38.277 --> 00:11:39.778
are you sure
you're okay with this?


00:11:39.912 --> 00:11:41.680
Thomas Michael Wachowski,


00:11:41.814 --> 00:11:44.216
what did you do the entire time
I was in veterinary school?


00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.819
I worked a second job
to pay the rent and...


00:11:46.953 --> 00:11:48.654
A third job to pay tuition.


00:11:48.787 --> 00:11:52.458
You sacrificed for me.
I'm happy to sacrifice for you.


00:11:53.826 --> 00:11:56.428
Babe, are you sure
you're okay with this?


00:11:57.496 --> 00:11:59.865
I mean, there's been
a Wachowski protecting this town


00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.167
for more than 50 years.


00:12:02.801 --> 00:12:04.536
This is a big change.


00:12:05.204 --> 00:12:07.306
I'm positive.


00:12:07.439 --> 00:12:10.242
It's time for this guy to
get out there and prove himself.


00:12:10.376 --> 00:12:12.244
I love Green Hills, but,


00:12:12.378 --> 00:12:14.014
you know, I want to help
people in real trouble.


00:12:14.146 --> 00:12:17.449
I want someone to turn to me
in a life-and-death situation


00:12:17.583 --> 00:12:19.318
and I'll be there for 'em.


00:12:20.152 --> 00:12:21.186
I get it.


00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:24.423
- I'm so proud of you.
- Thank you.


00:12:24.556 --> 00:12:25.491
Mmm!


00:12:25.624 --> 00:12:27.292
And so it is with a heavy heart,


00:12:27.426 --> 00:12:29.428
that I tell you all
that I've accepted a position


00:12:29.561 --> 00:12:31.363
at the San Francisco
Police Department,


00:12:31.497 --> 00:12:33.198
effective immediately.


00:12:33.332 --> 00:12:35.101
It's gonna be tough
to leave my hometown


00:12:35.234 --> 00:12:36.902
and all my friendships.


00:12:37.037 --> 00:12:40.806
But this is something
I feel like I need to do...


00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.274
to grow...


00:12:42.408 --> 00:12:46.245
as both an officer and a man.


00:12:48.414 --> 00:12:50.549
What do you think,
Sergeant Sprinkles?


00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:53.352
That wasn't so bad, right?


00:12:54.353 --> 00:12:56.388
Now all I got to do is...


00:12:57.189 --> 00:12:58.992
tell everyone
who isn't a donut.


00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:03.362
Whoa, the playoffs!


00:13:46.805 --> 00:13:49.641
Oh! So cool.


00:13:54.413 --> 00:13:55.481
Bottom of the ninth,
tie score.


00:13:55.614 --> 00:13:57.183
And exactly who you want
at the plate


00:13:57.316 --> 00:13:59.185
with the game
on the line: Sonic!


00:13:59.318 --> 00:14:00.886
But staring him down
from the pitcher's mound


00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.323
is the most fearsome southpaw
in Green Hills:


00:14:04.456 --> 00:14:05.691
Also Sonic.


00:14:05.824 --> 00:14:07.893
Okay. Focus, Sonic.
If you win this game,


00:14:08.027 --> 00:14:10.662
you'll be the most beloved kid
in Green Hills.


00:14:15.068 --> 00:14:18.570
Hit it to the guy in left!
He's a real space case.


00:14:21.507 --> 00:14:23.408
I can't with that guy.


00:14:23.542 --> 00:14:25.011
Hey, batter Sonic.
Hey, batter Sonic.


00:14:25.145 --> 00:14:27.880
"Suh-wing," batter Sonic.


00:14:35.354 --> 00:14:36.889
I got it, I got it, I got it!


00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.324
I don't got it.


00:14:48.168 --> 00:14:50.069
Go home! Go home!


00:14:50.402 --> 00:14:51.938
Come on!


00:14:56.943 --> 00:14:57.910
Safe!


00:14:59.845 --> 00:15:02.748
Yes!
Yes, yes, yes, yes! I did it!


00:15:02.881 --> 00:15:05.952
Did you see that?
I did it. I did it.


00:15:19.065 --> 00:15:21.000
I really am alone.


00:15:21.533 --> 00:15:24.436
All alone. Forever.


00:15:58.403 --> 00:16:01.941
I'm sure no one noticed that
giant blue explosion, right?


00:16:12.218 --> 00:16:13.619
- Hey, Wade.
- Hi, Tom.


00:16:13.752 --> 00:16:15.454
Uh, Wade here.


00:16:15.587 --> 00:16:17.257
What is going on?


00:16:17.389 --> 00:16:18.690
Well, gosh,
I think the power's out.


00:16:18.824 --> 00:16:20.626
Yeah, no dur!
The lights are out.


00:16:20.759 --> 00:16:22.594
The whole town is freaking out.


00:16:22.728 --> 00:16:24.663
- What should I do?
- <i>Okay, relax.</i>


00:16:24.796 --> 00:16:26.598
Take a deep breath, call Gil,


00:16:26.732 --> 00:16:29.335
see if they can locate
the downed line, then...


00:16:29.468 --> 00:16:32.338
call Zim and see if he can get
his generator over to the Super Q


00:16:32.471 --> 00:16:33.639
so the food stays... fresh.


00:16:33.772 --> 00:16:37.509
<i>Call Zim before Gil?</i>


00:16:37.643 --> 00:16:39.946
- <i>Call Gil... Hello?</i>
- I'll call you back.


00:16:40.079 --> 00:16:42.382
Wait! Hello? Was that
the end of the instructions?


00:16:43.815 --> 00:16:46.785
Okay, all right.
Uh, you can do this.


00:16:46.919 --> 00:16:51.024
What was the first thing
he said to do?


00:16:52.524 --> 00:16:54.826
Right. Relax.


00:17:14.813 --> 00:17:16.715
Twenty minutes ago,
an energy surge


00:17:16.848 --> 00:17:19.451
knocked out power across
the entire Pacific Northwest.


00:17:19.584 --> 00:17:20.752
What do we know?


00:17:20.886 --> 00:17:23.722
Well, our first instinct
was it was an EMP.


00:17:23.855 --> 00:17:26.591
But electromagnetic pulses
don't have that kind of power.


00:17:26.725 --> 00:17:29.128
NASA has ruled out
meteor strikes or solar flares.


00:17:29.262 --> 00:17:31.730
The Department of Energy says it's
not a power plant malfunction.


00:17:31.863 --> 00:17:33.333
Well, sounds like
we're really good


00:17:33.465 --> 00:17:34.700
at figuring out
what it wasn't.


00:17:34.833 --> 00:17:37.003
This could be a prelude
to a larger attack.


00:17:37.136 --> 00:17:39.238
I'm suggesting we scramble
the Fifth and Sixth Regiment.


00:17:39.372 --> 00:17:40.539
No, no, no, no.


00:17:40.672 --> 00:17:43.042
This needs a much more
sophisticated mind.


00:17:43.176 --> 00:17:44.944
Someone who
understands technology.


00:17:45.078 --> 00:17:48.014
- You want to send in a lab rat?
- Not just any lab rat.


00:17:48.147 --> 00:17:49.282
A lab rat with teeth.


00:17:49.415 --> 00:17:51.683
You're not suggesting
who I think you're suggesting.


00:17:51.817 --> 00:17:53.552
- I know, he's a little weird.
- Weird?


00:17:53.685 --> 00:17:56.055
- No. No way.
- He's a psychological tire fire!


00:17:56.189 --> 00:17:59.658
But he's also brilliant.
Five PhDs, IQ off the charts.


00:17:59.791 --> 00:18:02.462
And his drone tech
is revolutionary!


00:18:02.594 --> 00:18:04.430
You're sure he can handle this?


00:18:04.563 --> 00:18:06.432
He has a perfect
operations record.


00:18:06.565 --> 00:18:08.434
- Remember the coup in Pakistan?
- No.


00:18:08.567 --> 00:18:09.868
Or the uprising
in Azerbaijanistan?


00:18:10.003 --> 00:18:12.005
- That's not even a country.
- Exactly.


00:18:12.138 --> 00:18:14.240
And you can thank
Robotnik for that.


00:18:14.374 --> 00:18:17.609
I can't believe you're
bringing that freak into this.


00:18:17.743 --> 00:18:20.246
Neither can I, but...


00:18:21.147 --> 00:18:22.415
we have no choice.


00:18:48.107 --> 00:18:49.042
What the...


00:19:10.997 --> 00:19:12.432
Are you in charge here?


00:19:12.564 --> 00:19:13.632
- Yes, I am...
- Nope!


00:19:13.765 --> 00:19:14.633
- My...
- Wrong!


00:19:14.766 --> 00:19:16.169
- name...
- I'm in charge!


00:19:16.302 --> 00:19:17.503
- is Major...
- Me!


00:19:17.636 --> 00:19:19.905
- Ben...
- I'm in charge.


00:19:20.973 --> 00:19:22.975
You've never seen
anything like this before.


00:19:23.575 --> 00:19:24.944
It says
I'm the top banana


00:19:25.078 --> 00:19:27.679
in a world full of
hungry little monkeys.


00:19:27.813 --> 00:19:30.049
Allow me to clarify.


00:19:30.183 --> 00:19:31.517
In a sequentially
ranked hierarchy


00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.918
based on level
of critical importance,


00:19:33.052 --> 00:19:35.021
the disparity between us
is too vast to quantify.


00:19:35.154 --> 00:19:37.523
- Agent Stone?
- The Doctor thinks you're basic.


00:19:37.656 --> 00:19:39.658
I'm initiating a sweep sequence.


00:19:39.791 --> 00:19:42.395
Ten miles in every direction
should suffice.


00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.932
- Is he still looking at me funny?
- Yes, he is.


00:19:46.065 --> 00:19:47.766
Tell him to stop or I'll
pull up his search history.


00:19:47.899 --> 00:19:49.601
If you don't stop looking
at the Doctor,


00:19:49.734 --> 00:19:51.204
- he'll take a closer look...
- I'm not deaf.


00:19:51.337 --> 00:19:53.106
And tell him his men
report to me now.


00:19:53.239 --> 00:19:54.407
Blah-blah-blah.


00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.076
Excuse me? Listen, pal,
I don't know if you realize...


00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.212
I'm sorry, Major.
What was your name?


00:19:59.345 --> 00:20:01.713
- Benning...
- Nobody cares!


00:20:01.847 --> 00:20:05.184
Nobody cares. Listen,
Major Nobody Cares.


00:20:05.318 --> 00:20:07.487
You know why
nobody cares who you are?


00:20:07.619 --> 00:20:10.056
Because nobody cares about
your feeble accomplishments.


00:20:10.189 --> 00:20:13.025
And nobody cares
how proud your mommy is


00:20:13.159 --> 00:20:15.694
that you're now reading
at a third-grade level.


00:20:15.827 --> 00:20:17.930
- Mmm.
- Have you finished <i>Charlotte's Web</i> yet?


00:20:18.064 --> 00:20:20.199
Spoiler alert:
She dies in the end.


00:20:20.333 --> 00:20:22.502
But she leaves
a big creepy egg sac.


00:20:24.303 --> 00:20:26.973
Ah... my babies.


00:20:27.106 --> 00:20:30.042
Whoo! Look what came out
of my egg sac.


00:20:30.176 --> 00:20:32.945
You know what I love
about machines?


00:20:33.079 --> 00:20:36.616
They do what they're told.
They follow their programming.


00:20:36.748 --> 00:20:38.817
They don't need time off
to get drunk


00:20:38.951 --> 00:20:40.685
and put the boat in the water.


00:20:40.819 --> 00:20:42.421
Now you do what you're told.


00:20:42.555 --> 00:20:45.558
Stand over there on the edge
of your personal abyss...


00:20:46.325 --> 00:20:48.827
and watch my machines
do your job.


00:20:51.197 --> 00:20:53.698
- Can you feel it, Stone?
- I can feel it, Doctor.


00:20:53.832 --> 00:20:57.136
It's evolution, Stone.


00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.770
It's evolution!


00:21:34.574 --> 00:21:36.609
- Agent Stone?
- Doctor.


00:21:36.741 --> 00:21:38.877
Do you see anything useful
in this image?


00:21:39.911 --> 00:21:42.415
- Nothing at all, Doctor.
- Of course you don't.


00:21:42.548 --> 00:21:44.584
Your eyes weren't
expertly trained to spot tracks


00:21:44.716 --> 00:21:47.320
by the Native-American
Shadow Wolves.


00:21:57.363 --> 00:21:58.397
That's extraordinary.


00:21:58.531 --> 00:22:01.100
No. What's extraordinary is,


00:22:01.234 --> 00:22:03.102
I've determined
the exact height, weight


00:22:03.236 --> 00:22:04.803
and spinal curvature
of this creature,


00:22:04.937 --> 00:22:07.273
and my computer
can't find a single match for it


00:22:07.406 --> 00:22:10.276
anywhere in Earth's
animal kingdom.


00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:13.446
This blackout
was not a terrorist attack,


00:22:13.579 --> 00:22:15.648
and that's no baby bigfoot.


00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:19.418
This guy is something else...


00:22:20.586 --> 00:22:22.154
entirely.


00:22:22.288 --> 00:22:25.291
Divert all search units
to the site of the footprint.


00:22:26.058 --> 00:22:28.594
That's one small step for man,


00:22:28.728 --> 00:22:31.197
one giant leap for me.


00:22:42.174 --> 00:22:44.110
Okay, okay, everything is fine.


00:22:44.243 --> 00:22:46.245
You played some baseball,
got a little upset,


00:22:46.379 --> 00:22:49.582
lightning shot out of your butt,
and now they're coming for you.


00:22:50.650 --> 00:22:52.618
All right, all right.
Earth isn't safe anymore.


00:22:52.752 --> 00:22:54.420
Time for plan B.
Mushroomville.


00:22:54.553 --> 00:22:57.323
But I gotta take my stuff.
Okay, essential items only.


00:22:57.456 --> 00:22:59.858
Okay, toothbrush, toothpaste,
hair gel, night-light.


00:22:59.992 --> 00:23:01.961
Funny hat.
This half-eaten cantaloupe.


00:23:02.094 --> 00:23:03.929
Oh, and my scented candle.


00:23:04.063 --> 00:23:06.065
My entire comic book collection.
Bean bag chair.


00:23:06.198 --> 00:23:07.799
Can a bean bag chair
fit in a backpack?


00:23:07.933 --> 00:23:09.535
No, no, no. Of course not.
That's stupid.


00:23:09.669 --> 00:23:13.939
Okay, what else? The rings!
The rings, yes, of course.


00:23:14.906 --> 00:23:16.175
Here we go. Ring time.


00:23:16.309 --> 00:23:18.810
Mushroom planet, here I come.


00:23:18.944 --> 00:23:20.179
Oh, no.
They're right outside.


00:23:20.313 --> 00:23:23.316
I gotta go somewhere else.


00:23:26.786 --> 00:23:28.554
Goodbye, cave.


00:23:32.625 --> 00:23:34.293
- Hey.
- <i>Hey.</i>


00:23:34.427 --> 00:23:35.294
Whatcha doing?


00:23:35.428 --> 00:23:37.829
Just coloring
with Jojo and Rachel.


00:23:37.963 --> 00:23:39.965
Ah, that sounds...
half-fun.


00:23:40.099 --> 00:23:42.168
Hey, exciting stuff here.
We had a power outage.


00:23:42.301 --> 00:23:44.136
The whole town went dark.


00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.472
It was like a sign telling me
to get out of Dodge.


00:23:46.605 --> 00:23:48.774
- Wade must have lost his mind.
- <i>Yeah.</i>


00:23:48.907 --> 00:23:51.177
And he does not
have much to lose.


00:23:51.310 --> 00:23:53.746
How's your sister?
Did she convince you to leave me yet?


00:23:53.912 --> 00:23:57.216
No, but she did tell me to check
your phone for dating apps.


00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.352
<i>The only apps on my phone
are the ones that came with it.</i>


00:23:59.485 --> 00:24:01.387
- And the Olive Garden.
- <i>Ah.</i>


00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.422
- Because when you're there...
- You're family.


00:24:05.857 --> 00:24:07.326
No way.


00:24:09.762 --> 00:24:10.930
The raccoons are back.


00:24:11.063 --> 00:24:12.897
And they are in for a surprise.


00:24:13.032 --> 00:24:15.501
Your surprise better not be
my tranquilizer gun.


00:24:15.634 --> 00:24:16.569
They're just hungry.


00:24:16.702 --> 00:24:19.939
<i>And also, that's for bears.</i>


00:24:20.072 --> 00:24:22.241
- Good. Now I know it'll work.
- <i>Tom!</i>


00:24:22.375 --> 00:24:24.610
I'm kidding. I'm just gonna
use it to scare 'em.


00:24:24.744 --> 00:24:25.877
Possibly to death.


00:24:26.011 --> 00:24:27.279
- <i>Love you, honey, bye!</i>
- Tom...


00:24:32.051 --> 00:24:34.487
D-I-V-O-R-C-E.


00:24:36.822 --> 00:24:38.057
Okay, I'm in.


00:24:38.190 --> 00:24:41.060
With minimal damage
to Donut Lord's property.


00:24:41.761 --> 00:24:42.962
Here we go.


00:24:43.095 --> 00:24:44.296
It didn't work out on Earth,
but that's okay.


00:24:44.430 --> 00:24:45.798
You're going to a safe world.


00:24:45.931 --> 00:24:48.267
A nice, safe world
full of mushrooms.


00:24:48.401 --> 00:24:51.670
Mushrooms that'll be
your only friends.


00:24:51.804 --> 00:24:53.472
That sounds awful.
I can't do this.


00:24:53.606 --> 00:24:56.075
You have to do it.
There's no other option.


00:24:56.842 --> 00:24:59.145
All right.


00:25:00.546 --> 00:25:02.815
SFPD...
pending background check.


00:25:02.948 --> 00:25:04.583
Paws in the air!


00:25:06.352 --> 00:25:08.788
Uh, meow?


00:25:14.293 --> 00:25:15.561
Ow!


00:25:17.196 --> 00:25:20.533
"San... Francisco?"


00:25:42.621 --> 00:25:45.257
No.


00:25:48.661 --> 00:25:50.329
What?


00:26:12.618 --> 00:26:14.386
The blue devil.


00:26:27.299 --> 00:26:29.702
- Donut Lord?
- It can talk.


00:26:30.202 --> 00:26:31.303
You're not...


00:26:31.437 --> 00:26:32.705
You're not here
to abduct me, are you?


00:26:32.838 --> 00:26:34.406
You abducted me.


00:26:35.641 --> 00:26:37.910
Okay, that's a fair point.
What are you?


00:26:38.043 --> 00:26:39.845
Why are you hiding out
in my garage?


00:26:39.980 --> 00:26:41.380
I needed somewhere safe.


00:26:41.514 --> 00:26:43.549
And you're the only person
I could think of, Donut Lord.


00:26:43.682 --> 00:26:45.050
Why do you keep
calling me Donut Lord?


00:26:45.184 --> 00:26:46.418
'Cause you talk to donuts.


00:26:46.552 --> 00:26:48.654
And then eat them
if they get out of line.


00:26:48.787 --> 00:26:50.022
Again, fair.


00:26:50.155 --> 00:26:51.257
Wait, wait, wait.
Where are all the mushrooms?


00:26:51.390 --> 00:26:52.959
Why am I still on Earth?
What is...


00:26:53.092 --> 00:26:55.794
Oh, no!
I lost my rings.


00:26:55.929 --> 00:26:57.096
What?


00:27:02.868 --> 00:27:05.638
What's happening?
Is this your mother ship?


00:27:06.338 --> 00:27:07.706
I'm not in the mood
to get probed.


00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:10.709
You think you're worried?
I'm not even wearing pants.


00:27:14.146 --> 00:27:16.215
What the...


00:27:16.348 --> 00:27:19.251
- They're coming for me!
- Who's coming for you?


00:27:19.385 --> 00:27:21.287
- What's that got to do with me?
- I don't have time to explain,


00:27:21.420 --> 00:27:22.555
but you have to help me.


00:27:22.688 --> 00:27:24.490
No, I don't. Why?


00:27:24.623 --> 00:27:27.092
Well, my legs,
which normally would be classified


00:27:27.226 --> 00:27:29.328
as lethal weapons,
feel like spaghetti.


00:27:29.461 --> 00:27:32.531
I need your help. Please.
It's life or death.


00:27:40.272 --> 00:27:42.141
Fine. Come with me.


00:27:44.810 --> 00:27:46.845
Uh, little help?


00:27:58.058 --> 00:27:59.926
All right, stay here.
And be quiet.


00:28:00.060 --> 00:28:01.193
Good plan. Great plan!


00:28:01.327 --> 00:28:02.595
We're already working
so well together.


00:28:02.728 --> 00:28:05.531
Practically finishing
each other's sentences.


00:28:06.732 --> 00:28:08.133
Okay, bye.


00:28:11.236 --> 00:28:12.705
Hello there!


00:28:13.372 --> 00:28:14.707
Can I help you?


00:28:18.310 --> 00:28:20.879
Good morning,
my rural chum.


00:28:21.014 --> 00:28:24.683
I'm... from the power company,
investigating the blackout.


00:28:24.817 --> 00:28:26.685
If you don't mind,
I'd like to take a few readings


00:28:26.819 --> 00:28:28.153
inside your house?


00:28:28.287 --> 00:28:29.755
No kidding?
You're from the power company?


00:28:29.888 --> 00:28:31.457
- Mmm.
- Oh, you must know my buddy Spencer.


00:28:31.590 --> 00:28:34.560
- We play softball together.
- Ah! Spence.


00:28:35.095 --> 00:28:37.196
He's a good man.


00:28:37.329 --> 00:28:40.000
- Yeah. Come on in!
- Great.


00:28:40.132 --> 00:28:41.567
Take all the readings you need.


00:28:41.700 --> 00:28:43.335
Except, uh...


00:28:43.469 --> 00:28:46.338
Doesn't the power company usually take
their readings from outside the house?


00:28:46.472 --> 00:28:49.174
That way they can check them
even if you're not home.


00:28:49.308 --> 00:28:51.510
Also, my buddy Spencer
works for the gas company,


00:28:51.644 --> 00:28:53.245
and he's more of
an Ultimate Frisbee guy.


00:28:53.379 --> 00:28:56.016
So you want to tell me
why you think I'm dumb enough


00:28:56.148 --> 00:28:57.816
to just let you
walk inside my house?


00:29:06.458 --> 00:29:08.861
- I'm sorry, Mister...
- Wachowski.


00:29:08.995 --> 00:29:10.629
But everyone calls me Tom.


00:29:10.763 --> 00:29:12.598
Except my dentist,
he calls me Tim.


00:29:12.731 --> 00:29:14.199
But it's gone on
for so long now


00:29:14.333 --> 00:29:16.301
that it would just be weird
if I corrected him.


00:29:16.435 --> 00:29:18.537
Well, Tom, whose-dentist-
calls-him-Tim.


00:29:18.671 --> 00:29:20.572
You may have noticed
that this entire town


00:29:20.706 --> 00:29:22.374
has been experiencing
a power outage.


00:29:22.508 --> 00:29:24.276
Yep, no lights.
Picked up on that.


00:29:24.410 --> 00:29:27.446
Twenty minutes ago, I tracked an
energy pulse with a similar signature


00:29:27.579 --> 00:29:29.848
to the one that caused
that disruption.


00:29:44.563 --> 00:29:46.632
Listen, uh, Mister...


00:29:46.765 --> 00:29:47.800
Doctor.


00:29:47.934 --> 00:29:50.803
Dr. Robotnik.
But my dentist calls me Rob.


00:29:50.937 --> 00:29:52.438
Hmm.


00:29:52.571 --> 00:29:55.808
Look, uh, Dr. Robotskeez.


00:29:55.942 --> 00:29:58.144
Um, I'm sure what you're
here for is very serious,


00:29:58.277 --> 00:29:59.511
but it's got nothing
to do with me.


00:29:59.645 --> 00:30:01.014
You can ask anyone in town.


00:30:01.147 --> 00:30:03.049
- Everyone knows me.
- I bet they do.


00:30:03.183 --> 00:30:04.416
I'm sure you're hella popular


00:30:04.550 --> 00:30:06.318
with the Jebs and Merles
and Billy Bobs,


00:30:06.452 --> 00:30:08.854
in this glorified
gas-station rest stop.


00:30:08.988 --> 00:30:11.223
Betcha go way back
to the days of tippin' cows


00:30:11.356 --> 00:30:13.225
and playin' in a jug band!


00:30:16.261 --> 00:30:18.932
And maybe someday
you'll achieve your goal


00:30:19.065 --> 00:30:21.734
of getting a Costco card
or adopting a Labradoodle.


00:30:21.867 --> 00:30:24.204
But the reality is,
I surpassed


00:30:24.336 --> 00:30:27.773
everything you're
ever going to do...


00:30:29.308 --> 00:30:30.977
before I was a toddler.


00:30:31.111 --> 00:30:34.913
I was spitting out formulas while
you were still spitting up formula.


00:30:35.048 --> 00:30:36.281
I was breastfed,
actually.


00:30:36.415 --> 00:30:39.651
Nice.
Rub that in my orphan face.


00:30:40.385 --> 00:30:42.488
Mr. Wachowski,
are you familiar with


00:30:42.621 --> 00:30:46.226
US Code 904,
Title 10, Article 104?


00:30:46.825 --> 00:30:48.694
- Yeah, who isn't...
- "Anyone...


00:30:48.827 --> 00:30:52.664
who attempts to aid an enemy of the
United States shall suffer death."


00:30:53.766 --> 00:30:56.335
And if I'm the one
that catches you,


00:30:56.468 --> 00:30:57.870
it'll be even worse.


00:30:59.905 --> 00:31:01.107
Worse than death?


00:31:03.442 --> 00:31:04.743
Okay, I'm a ball,
a normal ball.


00:31:04.877 --> 00:31:06.345
I'm blending in like a ball.


00:31:06.478 --> 00:31:07.746
Shh. Stop talking.
No, <i>you</i> stop talking.


00:31:07.880 --> 00:31:09.748
Be quiet, Sonic.
<i>You</i> be quiet, Sonic.


00:31:09.882 --> 00:31:12.484
Oh, I hope they aren't
scanning me with X-rays.


00:31:12.618 --> 00:31:14.653
I had kind of
an embarrassing lunch.


00:31:22.494 --> 00:31:24.763
Don't freak out. Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.


00:31:24.897 --> 00:31:27.633
Don't freak out. Don't freak out.
Don't freak out.


00:31:28.134 --> 00:31:30.335
I'm freaking out!


00:31:31.904 --> 00:31:34.207
Why don't you have
your staircase carpeted?


00:31:34.339 --> 00:31:36.441
Compared to what I...


00:31:39.012 --> 00:31:40.445
- Old pipes.
- Yeah.


00:31:40.579 --> 00:31:42.081
Probably just
the house settling.


00:31:42.215 --> 00:31:43.983
Nothing to see here!


00:31:45.151 --> 00:31:46.418
Hey!


00:31:51.456 --> 00:31:53.026
Here's the thing.


00:31:54.493 --> 00:31:56.428
I'm never wrong.


00:31:56.562 --> 00:31:59.032
Well, first time
for everything, I guess.


00:31:59.165 --> 00:32:00.399
Would you like some cake?


00:32:00.532 --> 00:32:01.834
I hear raccoons have
the cleanest mouths


00:32:01.968 --> 00:32:03.869
of any animal that
routinely eats garbage.


00:32:16.249 --> 00:32:17.984
Look at that.


00:32:18.517 --> 00:32:20.286
I was right.


00:32:20.419 --> 00:32:22.554
Note the lack of surprise.


00:32:22.688 --> 00:32:24.356
Shall we try this again?


00:32:34.766 --> 00:32:38.171
I'm going to give you five
seconds to tell me where it is.


00:32:38.304 --> 00:32:39.438
Five...


00:32:39.571 --> 00:32:40.639
I don't know what
you're talking about.


00:32:40.772 --> 00:32:41.807
- Four.
- Hey, tough guy. I'm a cop,


00:32:41.941 --> 00:32:43.408
and you're
threatening an officer.


00:32:43.542 --> 00:32:45.711
How can you threaten somebody
who never existed?


00:32:45.844 --> 00:32:47.113
Three...


00:32:47.247 --> 00:32:48.847
Come on!
Rack your brain.


00:32:48.982 --> 00:32:51.284
You might be able to come up
with some lame excuse


00:32:51.416 --> 00:32:53.987
to go on living
in two...


00:32:54.954 --> 00:32:56.022
one.


00:32:56.655 --> 00:32:58.091
Wait! Don't hurt him!


00:33:12.071 --> 00:33:13.739
This feels excessive.


00:33:17.243 --> 00:33:18.577
Stay behind me.


00:33:32.125 --> 00:33:33.558
Hiya!


00:33:34.559 --> 00:33:36.930
Don't worry. I got it
right where I want it!


00:33:39.531 --> 00:33:43.002
Can you believe Amazon is gonna
deliver packages with these things?


00:33:45.537 --> 00:33:48.573
This was a horrible plan!
What was I thinking?


00:33:50.676 --> 00:33:52.511
I'm gonna puke!


00:33:56.448 --> 00:33:59.018
Come on!
We gotta get out of here.


00:33:59.152 --> 00:34:01.220
Oh, don't tell me
that's all you got!


00:34:01.354 --> 00:34:02.721
I'm just getting started!


00:34:02.854 --> 00:34:05.091
Let me know if you want to go
round two with the blue.


00:34:24.509 --> 00:34:26.611
Doctor! Are you okay?


00:34:26.745 --> 00:34:29.215
I saw a guy race out of here
and thought...


00:34:29.349 --> 00:34:31.150
That you should
stop them?


00:34:32.151 --> 00:34:33.618
Open your mouth...


00:34:33.752 --> 00:34:35.620
and say you thought that you
should stop them.


00:34:35.754 --> 00:34:37.457
No, I thought that maybe
I should check


00:34:37.589 --> 00:34:39.225
to see if you were okay...


00:34:39.359 --> 00:34:41.860
You know what's hard about being
the smartest person in the world?


00:34:41.995 --> 00:34:45.264
- Everyone else seems stupid.
- Stupid, yes! Way to go!


00:34:45.398 --> 00:34:46.732
You got that one.


00:34:48.067 --> 00:34:51.938
Whatever this creature is,
it's our job to secure it,


00:34:52.071 --> 00:34:56.142
neutralize it,
uncover the source of its power.


00:34:56.275 --> 00:34:57.843
And if it resists,


00:34:58.643 --> 00:35:00.113
we take it apart...


00:35:00.746 --> 00:35:02.581
piece by piece.


00:35:03.515 --> 00:35:05.218
See what makes it tick.


00:35:06.486 --> 00:35:07.686
- Stone?
- Doctor?


00:35:07.819 --> 00:35:10.189
Call Optical Illusions.


00:35:10.323 --> 00:35:12.458
Tell them I need new frames.


00:35:12.591 --> 00:35:14.593
They know what kind I like.


00:35:14.726 --> 00:35:17.230
Oh, and bring that quill.


00:35:18.364 --> 00:35:19.831
Yes, Doctor.


00:35:22.768 --> 00:35:23.936
All right, pal,


00:35:24.070 --> 00:35:25.570
you need to start talking
right now.


00:35:25.704 --> 00:35:27.974
Who are you? What are you?


00:35:28.107 --> 00:35:30.742
I'm a hedgehog!
I feel like that's obvious.


00:35:30.876 --> 00:35:33.446
- And I'm in big trouble.
- Oh, <i>you're</i> in big trouble?


00:35:33.578 --> 00:35:35.982
You're not the one who punched some
sort of government weirdo back there.


00:35:36.115 --> 00:35:38.884
You think <i>you</i> have problems?
I lost my rings.


00:35:39.018 --> 00:35:40.453
Rings?
What are you talking about?


00:35:40.585 --> 00:35:43.056
Okay. Rings are how
all advanced cultures


00:35:43.189 --> 00:35:44.524
travel between worlds.


00:35:44.656 --> 00:35:46.959
And now mine are
on top of a pointy building


00:35:47.093 --> 00:35:50.530
- I've only ever seen on your skintight T-shirt.
- Hey.


00:35:50.662 --> 00:35:52.564
So, I'd like you to take me
to San Francisco,


00:35:52.697 --> 00:35:54.467
so I can get back my rings
and use them


00:35:54.599 --> 00:35:56.135
to go to the mushroom planet.


00:35:57.569 --> 00:35:59.805
- Mushroom planet.
- Yes!


00:36:00.406 --> 00:36:01.773
Right.


00:36:05.211 --> 00:36:07.846
- Okay, pal, out you go.
- I'm sorry, what?


00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:09.848
Look, this is
the worst possible time


00:36:09.982 --> 00:36:11.817
for me to get myself
into trouble, okay?


00:36:11.951 --> 00:36:13.986
You asked me to save your life,
I saved your life.


00:36:14.120 --> 00:36:17.190
Now, please, go find your rings.
And your mushroom land.


00:36:17.323 --> 00:36:18.991
Hopefully I'm gonna wake up
in a hospital bed


00:36:19.125 --> 00:36:21.094
and the doctor's gonna tell me
that my colonoscopy


00:36:21.227 --> 00:36:23.362
was a big success, okay?
So goodbye.


00:36:23.496 --> 00:36:26.731
- Okay. Goodbye.
- Goodbye.


00:36:28.633 --> 00:36:31.736
- Why aren't you leaving?
- I don't know where San Francisco is.


00:36:31.870 --> 00:36:32.871
- It's west.
- West?


00:36:33.005 --> 00:36:34.207
Straight shot, can't miss it.


00:36:34.340 --> 00:36:35.408
Fine. That's cool.


00:36:35.541 --> 00:36:37.609
I'm totally cool
saying goodbye now.


00:36:42.248 --> 00:36:46.552
So, as I crashed into the cold,
dark water of the Pacific,


00:36:46.685 --> 00:36:48.920
I realized a few things.


00:36:49.055 --> 00:36:51.424
A, I have no idea
where I'm going.


00:36:51.557 --> 00:36:53.493
B, saltwater stings.


00:36:53.625 --> 00:36:58.197
C, I shouldn't even be on
this planet right now, but I am.


00:36:58.331 --> 00:37:00.166
Why? Because you shot me!


00:37:00.299 --> 00:37:01.968
- I know.
- You shot me!


00:37:02.101 --> 00:37:03.668
All right, I heard you
the first time.


00:37:03.802 --> 00:37:06.372
You don't have to pile it on.
Good grief.


00:37:06.506 --> 00:37:09.342
I'm wet. I'm cold.


00:37:09.475 --> 00:37:11.110
There's a fish on my head!


00:37:11.244 --> 00:37:14.846
And clearly, I'm not gonna
be able to do this on my own.


00:37:19.185 --> 00:37:21.786
All right,
get in the truck.


00:37:21.920 --> 00:37:23.589
Really? You're gonna help me?


00:37:23.722 --> 00:37:26.192
I guess it is a little bit my fault
that all this is happening to you.


00:37:26.325 --> 00:37:29.362
Not a little bit. Entirely.
It is entirely your fault.


00:37:29.495 --> 00:37:31.998
Okay, it's entirely my fault.
Are you coming?


00:37:32.131 --> 00:37:33.199
Yes.


00:37:35.535 --> 00:37:36.902
Road trip! Whoop-whoop!


00:37:37.036 --> 00:37:38.971
What am I doing?


00:37:40.039 --> 00:37:41.641
All right, there's
gonna be rules on this trip.


00:37:41.773 --> 00:37:44.577
Number one, do exactly
as I say all the time.


00:37:44.709 --> 00:37:46.711
- Got it?
- Got it, Donut Lord.


00:37:46.845 --> 00:37:49.282
Would you stop
with the "Donut Lord"?


00:37:49.415 --> 00:37:51.117
I have a name. It's Tom.


00:37:51.617 --> 00:37:52.518
I'm Sonic.


00:37:52.652 --> 00:37:55.154
Sonic. Sonic.


00:37:56.255 --> 00:37:58.690
So you've been
spying on us all for years.


00:37:58.823 --> 00:38:00.159
I wouldn't call it "spying."


00:38:00.293 --> 00:38:02.761
We were all just hanging out,
only I wasn't invited


00:38:02.894 --> 00:38:04.197
and no one knew I was there.


00:38:04.330 --> 00:38:06.599
I can't believe Crazy Carl
was right all this time.


00:38:06.731 --> 00:38:09.936
Yeah. You should call him
Super Observant Carl instead.


00:38:10.902 --> 00:38:12.972
- Oh, my God, stop the car right now!
- What? What?


00:38:13.105 --> 00:38:15.374
The World's Largest
Rubberband Ball?


00:38:15.508 --> 00:38:17.410
- We gotta see it!
- No. No.


00:38:17.543 --> 00:38:20.213
No, this is not some
fun family road trip, okay?


00:38:20.346 --> 00:38:22.448
The government wants
to dissect you.


00:38:22.582 --> 00:38:24.350
And arrest me. This is serious.


00:38:25.750 --> 00:38:27.186
Eh, you're right, it was lame.


00:38:27.320 --> 00:38:29.788
Gift shop was cool, though.
I got you a mouse pad.


00:38:29.921 --> 00:38:31.591
When are we gonna get there?


00:38:31.723 --> 00:38:34.026
We will get there
when we get there.


00:38:52.744 --> 00:38:55.715
I'm gonna go check in with Wade,
see if he knows what's going on.


00:38:55.847 --> 00:38:58.184
You're gonna see Wade
in that glass thing?


00:38:58.317 --> 00:39:00.386
What is it, a teleportation box?


00:39:02.088 --> 00:39:03.956
It's a pay phone.
It's mostly for drug dealers


00:39:04.090 --> 00:39:06.459
and fugitives from the law,
which is us.


00:39:06.592 --> 00:39:08.427
Stay in the car.
I don't want anybody seeing you.


00:39:08.561 --> 00:39:10.762
Fine.


00:39:21.474 --> 00:39:22.341
Huh?


00:39:30.049 --> 00:39:31.783
Okay, okay.
That is the coolest place on Earth,


00:39:31.916 --> 00:39:33.953
but you have to stay in the car.


00:39:43.562 --> 00:39:45.931
Be strong. Be strong.


00:39:48.701 --> 00:39:49.935
Hmm.


00:39:52.871 --> 00:39:54.873
Hello.
Green Hills Police Department.


00:39:55.007 --> 00:39:56.742
- Wade, it's me.
- <i>Hi.</i>


00:39:56.875 --> 00:39:58.144
I'm so glad that you called.


00:39:58.277 --> 00:40:00.845
Uh, so, some guys came in
asking some questions.


00:40:00.980 --> 00:40:02.481
Uh, they're a little creepy.


00:40:02.615 --> 00:40:05.251
Kind of reminded me of
the guys from <i>Men in Black,</i>


00:40:05.384 --> 00:40:08.754
but not as likable
or charming as Will Smith.


00:40:08.887 --> 00:40:10.156
Wait, what kind of questions?


00:40:10.289 --> 00:40:13.426
Um, questions about terrorism?


00:40:13.559 --> 00:40:16.796
I told them that I've gone
ice fishing with Tom.


00:40:16.929 --> 00:40:18.197
He doesn't know how
to make a bomb.


00:40:18.331 --> 00:40:20.566
<i>He can't even
make bait in the cold.</i>


00:40:20.700 --> 00:40:22.802
All right, Wade, listen to me.
This is really important.


00:40:22.935 --> 00:40:24.570
Don't tell them
that we talked, okay?


00:40:28.007 --> 00:40:30.276
You know, I think
they already know.


00:40:32.278 --> 00:40:34.846
Mr. Wachowski.


00:40:35.247 --> 00:40:36.282
Tom.


00:40:36.415 --> 00:40:37.950
I want you to know
that the only other person


00:40:38.084 --> 00:40:41.153
who ever punched me in the face
was the school bully.


00:40:41.287 --> 00:40:43.855
He hit me in the cafeteria,
causing a blunt-force contusion


00:40:43.989 --> 00:40:46.425
to the soft tissue
surrounding my orbital bone.


00:40:46.559 --> 00:40:48.728
Humiliated me in front of
the entire school!


00:40:48.860 --> 00:40:50.463
And do you know
what I did in response?


00:40:50.596 --> 00:40:53.499
Uh, I'm assuming that you reported
him to the principal's office


00:40:53.632 --> 00:40:55.501
'cause that kind of behavior
is really unacceptable.


00:40:55.634 --> 00:40:58.971
No. I examined the inefficiency of
a world where brawn trumped brain


00:40:59.105 --> 00:41:02.007
and I used technology
to resolve that inefficiency.


00:41:02.141 --> 00:41:05.144
The boy ate his meals
through a straw for a year.


00:41:05.277 --> 00:41:07.279
And I have never
lost a fight again.


00:41:07.680 --> 00:41:08.614
Until today.


00:41:08.748 --> 00:41:10.282
Hey, hooray for me then, huh?


00:41:10.416 --> 00:41:13.152
No, because you're about to
become the bully with the straw!


00:41:13.285 --> 00:41:15.887
I'm coming for you,
Mr. Wachowski.


00:41:16.021 --> 00:41:17.556
And when I catch you, I'll...


00:41:18.023 --> 00:41:19.891
Hello.


00:41:20.025 --> 00:41:21.293
Hello?


00:41:21.827 --> 00:41:22.762
Hello, hello, hello?


00:41:22.894 --> 00:41:24.363
I think he actually hung up,


00:41:24.497 --> 00:41:26.031
because I notice
that the light isn't on.


00:41:26.165 --> 00:41:27.500
Thank you, Officer Brainfart.


00:41:27.633 --> 00:41:29.869
If you give me a second,
I can get an outside line.


00:41:30.002 --> 00:41:32.104
No. Don't be bothered.


00:41:32.238 --> 00:41:35.141
You just sit there and be "u"...


00:41:35.875 --> 00:41:37.410
...'seless.


00:41:44.250 --> 00:41:47.153
No one's gonna
erase my memory here?


00:41:48.087 --> 00:41:50.222
I will tell people about this!


00:41:52.758 --> 00:41:56.562
Okay, not exactly
the healthiest meal, but...


00:41:57.563 --> 00:41:58.631
Sonic?


00:42:02.735 --> 00:42:04.203
Oh, no.


00:42:04.737 --> 00:42:06.472
No, no, no, no, no!


00:42:10.976 --> 00:42:12.845
- Whoo!
- Yeah!


00:42:21.253 --> 00:42:22.555
Howdy, pardner!


00:42:22.688 --> 00:42:24.123
I'm not your partner.
Come on. We're leaving.


00:42:24.256 --> 00:42:25.858
But there's a ZZ Top cover band.


00:42:25.991 --> 00:42:27.593
You gotta see their beards.


00:42:27.726 --> 00:42:29.428
You're gonna have to catch 'em
some other time. Let's go. Get up!


00:42:29.562 --> 00:42:32.665
If we stay, I won't say another
word for the rest of the trip,


00:42:32.798 --> 00:42:34.467
starting... now.


00:42:35.668 --> 00:42:37.938
Welcome to the Piston Pit.
What can I get you fellas?


00:42:38.070 --> 00:42:40.239
I want nachos and buffalo wings,
oh, and guac.


00:42:40.372 --> 00:42:42.808
Funny word, isn't it?
Guac, guac! Guac.


00:42:42.943 --> 00:42:44.343
Hey, no kids
allowed in here.


00:42:44.477 --> 00:42:45.946
What's he got on,
some kind of mask?


00:42:46.078 --> 00:42:49.482
Oh, he's actually
43 years old and, um,


00:42:49.615 --> 00:42:51.517
suffers from
a very rare skin disease


00:42:51.650 --> 00:42:56.021
that stunts his growth and makes him
look, uh, like that.


00:42:56.155 --> 00:42:57.323
The face,
I was born with.


00:42:57.456 --> 00:42:59.825
The confidence,
I picked up along the way.


00:42:59.960 --> 00:43:02.963
- Make his a Mello Yello, please.
- Okay.


00:43:03.930 --> 00:43:06.765
- You owe me one.
- I never sat on a barstool before.


00:43:06.899 --> 00:43:08.200
So squishy!


00:43:08.334 --> 00:43:10.236
Oh, look at this.
It spins.


00:43:10.870 --> 00:43:11.938
- Yes.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:43:12.071 --> 00:43:13.873
- That's nice.
- I feel sick.


00:43:14.006 --> 00:43:15.241
Are you having fun?


00:43:15.374 --> 00:43:16.909
Gonna check this off
the ol' bucket list, huh?


00:43:17.042 --> 00:43:18.979
- Big night for you.
- What's a bucket list?


00:43:19.111 --> 00:43:21.714
A bucket list is, uh...


00:43:21.847 --> 00:43:24.450
It's a list of things
you want to do in your life


00:43:24.583 --> 00:43:27.019
before you, well,
kick the bucket.


00:43:27.152 --> 00:43:28.787
I've never
kicked a bucket, either!


00:43:28.921 --> 00:43:30.723
Oh, I gotta make my list.


00:43:33.292 --> 00:43:34.793
Uh-huh. Mm-hmm.


00:43:34.928 --> 00:43:37.263
Oh, Sonic!


00:43:37.897 --> 00:43:39.331
Uh-huh.


00:43:44.103 --> 00:43:45.271
What? What's the matter?


00:43:45.404 --> 00:43:47.606
There's so much stuff
I've never done.


00:43:47.740 --> 00:43:50.276
And now that I'm
leaving Earth forever,


00:43:50.409 --> 00:43:51.810
I guess I missed my chance.


00:43:57.816 --> 00:43:59.518
Well, I guess
this is the kind of place


00:43:59.652 --> 00:44:02.721
you could get a lot of living
done in a short period of time.


00:44:03.355 --> 00:44:04.490
I suppose we can spare an hour.


00:44:04.623 --> 00:44:07.192
What? You're gonna
bucket-list with me?


00:44:07.326 --> 00:44:10.129
- Sure, why not?
- You won't regret this.


00:44:10.262 --> 00:44:11.597
Oh, I'm pretty sure I will.


00:44:35.788 --> 00:44:37.756
New high score!


00:44:40.092 --> 00:44:41.794
Yippee-ki-yay!


00:44:42.227 --> 00:44:43.395
Ah-ha!


00:44:43.529 --> 00:44:45.431
Wait a second,
is this bull missing a head


00:44:45.564 --> 00:44:47.466
or does it have two butts?


00:44:49.368 --> 00:44:51.637
This is easy.


00:44:51.770 --> 00:44:54.607
- Okay.
- Ha-ha! Yeehaw!


00:44:57.376 --> 00:44:58.877
I'm a cowboy, baby!


00:45:02.082 --> 00:45:03.816
I'm okay.


00:45:06.285 --> 00:45:08.554
Whoo!


00:45:09.355 --> 00:45:11.057
Whoo! Yeah!


00:45:11.190 --> 00:45:13.192
Ha-ha-ha!


00:45:13.325 --> 00:45:14.493
Yeah, yeah, laugh it up.


00:45:14.627 --> 00:45:16.161
Nice work, Romeo.


00:45:16.295 --> 00:45:18.098
Glad you're having a good time.


00:45:18.230 --> 00:45:19.598
I am having a good time!


00:45:19.732 --> 00:45:22.768
I'm having the best time.
I mean, what could go wrong?


00:45:24.803 --> 00:45:26.205
Uh...


00:45:27.007 --> 00:45:28.240
Can we help you?


00:45:28.374 --> 00:45:30.010
We don't like
your kind around here.


00:45:30.142 --> 00:45:32.344
Our kind?
What kind is that?


00:45:34.213 --> 00:45:35.447
Hipsters.


00:45:35.581 --> 00:45:37.483
- How dare you.
- Oh, hey. You know what?


00:45:37.616 --> 00:45:38.952
We were leaving anyway.
Weren't we?


00:45:39.085 --> 00:45:41.487
- There's not a problem here.
- No, no, no, it's okay.


00:45:41.620 --> 00:45:42.821
No, no, no,
we're leaving.


00:45:42.956 --> 00:45:45.224
I know exactly
how to handle this situation.


00:45:45.357 --> 00:45:47.793
Pop quiz, hotshot.


00:45:47.927 --> 00:45:50.329
You just picked a fight with
a poorly disguised hedgehog


00:45:50.462 --> 00:45:52.498
who's seen way too many
action movies.


00:45:52.631 --> 00:45:55.101
What do you do? What do you do?


00:45:56.635 --> 00:45:59.538
Huh. Am I crazy?
It's supposed to break, right?


00:45:59.672 --> 00:46:02.541
Dink! Dink-dink!
Break, please. Break, please.


00:46:02.675 --> 00:46:04.077
Break this bottle, please.


00:46:04.209 --> 00:46:05.511
- Please, please, please.
- Uh, Sonic?


00:46:06.512 --> 00:46:07.947
Uh-oh!


00:46:16.122 --> 00:46:18.490
- Oh-ho-ho-ho!
- Nice going!


00:46:18.624 --> 00:46:20.526
Thanks! It's awesome right?


00:46:20.659 --> 00:46:22.095
All right, who's next?
Who wants some?


00:46:22.227 --> 00:46:23.963
Who do I get to beat up?


00:46:24.797 --> 00:46:26.632
Hey! Has anybody
seen my waitress?


00:46:26.765 --> 00:46:28.935
Still waiting on
those buffalo wings.


00:46:29.069 --> 00:46:31.670
Why, you!


00:46:34.840 --> 00:46:36.709
Ha-ha-ha!


00:46:38.178 --> 00:46:40.146
Uh-oh!


00:46:42.848 --> 00:46:43.849
Really?


00:48:15.674 --> 00:48:17.676
<i>Olé!</i>


00:48:33.159 --> 00:48:35.861
- So, should we get out of here?
- Yeah, time to go.


00:48:36.495 --> 00:48:39.265
That was amazing!


00:48:39.398 --> 00:48:40.967
Wait a second.
Did we even pay our tab?


00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:42.434
It doesn't matter!


00:48:42.568 --> 00:48:44.703
Watch this, watch this.
I always wanted to do this.


00:48:48.208 --> 00:48:50.843
- Get 'em!
- See ya, suckers!


00:48:50.977 --> 00:48:54.546
I can't say for sure,
but I think they liked me.


00:48:55.581 --> 00:48:57.416
Come on!
Don't let 'em get away!


00:48:59.085 --> 00:49:01.087
- Oh, yes!
- Yeah!


00:49:01.221 --> 00:49:02.421
- Yes!
- Ouch!


00:49:02.554 --> 00:49:03.622
He got you pretty good.


00:49:03.755 --> 00:49:04.958
I'm all right.
I've been hit harder.


00:49:05.091 --> 00:49:07.093
Did you see how much
toilet paper I used?


00:49:07.227 --> 00:49:10.596
The next person that goes into that
bathroom will have nothing to wipe with!


00:49:11.463 --> 00:49:13.565
The floors were sticky.
The crowd was rough.


00:49:13.699 --> 00:49:15.101
And the odds
were against us.


00:49:15.235 --> 00:49:18.537
But there was no stopping
Donut Lord and the Blue Blur.


00:49:18.670 --> 00:49:20.873
Scratch another one
off my list.


00:49:22.242 --> 00:49:24.710
You are a weird little dude.


00:49:32.718 --> 00:49:33.652
Mmm.


00:49:33.785 --> 00:49:34.686
Mmm.


00:49:34.820 --> 00:49:35.888
Mmm.


00:49:36.022 --> 00:49:36.822
Mmm.


00:49:36.956 --> 00:49:37.623
Okay.


00:49:37.756 --> 00:49:39.391
So what are we gonna do now?


00:49:40.893 --> 00:49:43.930
I'm gonna pass out watching TV.
I think you should too.


00:49:44.063 --> 00:49:45.631
But this is my
last night on Earth.


00:49:45.764 --> 00:49:47.300
I want to soak up
every last second.


00:49:47.432 --> 00:49:49.568
All right, well, anything you
can find to do in this room,


00:49:49.701 --> 00:49:50.937
you knock yourself out.


00:49:58.311 --> 00:49:59.745
Good times.


00:50:01.480 --> 00:50:03.849
Oh, come on.


00:50:03.983 --> 00:50:05.751
That's awful.
What did you eat?


00:50:05.884 --> 00:50:08.121
I think it's called a chili dog?


00:50:08.254 --> 00:50:11.090
You might want to check
your fur on that one, buddy.


00:50:12.191 --> 00:50:14.928
Hey. So, what's this next planet
you're supposed to go to like?


00:50:15.061 --> 00:50:17.462
It's no Earth,
I can tell you that.


00:50:17.596 --> 00:50:19.498
There's no people,
just breathable air


00:50:19.631 --> 00:50:21.633
and giant mushrooms and stuff.


00:50:22.201 --> 00:50:23.835
Well, look at it this way.


00:50:23.970 --> 00:50:26.838
At least you won't be
the only "fun-guy."


00:50:26.973 --> 00:50:29.042
No. Don't ever do that again.


00:50:30.442 --> 00:50:32.145
I liked it.


00:50:33.812 --> 00:50:36.015
I'm really gonna
miss this place.


00:50:36.149 --> 00:50:38.184
I know I have to
leave Earth to be safe,


00:50:38.318 --> 00:50:40.153
but what if
Longclaw was wrong?


00:50:41.020 --> 00:50:43.455
Maybe I could have a life here.


00:50:47.592 --> 00:50:50.529
All right.
We should get some sleep.


00:50:51.530 --> 00:50:52.932
You sleep.
Don't worry about me.


00:50:53.066 --> 00:50:56.568
I'm gonna stay up all night
enjoying Earth while I can.


00:50:57.070 --> 00:50:58.537
Sure, kid.


00:50:58.670 --> 00:51:01.040
As long as we're
on the road by 8:00.


00:51:07.180 --> 00:51:09.983
I ate a chili dog.
That's why my farts smell.


00:51:24.496 --> 00:51:29.235
<i>Thomas Wachowski, accused of committing
an act of domestic terrorism.</i>


00:51:29.369 --> 00:51:32.171
<i>Wachowski is considered
armed and dangerous.</i>


00:51:32.305 --> 00:51:34.140
<i>Any information
regarding his whereabouts</i>


00:51:34.273 --> 00:51:37.876
<i>should be reported to
local authorities immediately.</i>


00:51:43.548 --> 00:51:45.084
Did he say where he was going?


00:51:48.553 --> 00:51:51.190
Maybe. Maybe not.


00:51:51.923 --> 00:51:53.592
Like I'd ever tell you.


00:51:54.693 --> 00:51:56.561
Stand down, Agent Stone.


00:51:56.695 --> 00:52:00.599
This well-meaning citizen obviously doesn't
understand the urgency of the matter.


00:52:03.302 --> 00:52:04.569
Really?


00:52:07.440 --> 00:52:09.608
Now that's
what I call good cop, bad cop.


00:52:11.310 --> 00:52:12.744
Hoy!


00:52:12.878 --> 00:52:14.579
Left yourself open.


00:52:17.150 --> 00:52:18.884
Judging by the quickest route
to San Francisco,


00:52:19.018 --> 00:52:20.786
the approximate
speed of their vehicle,


00:52:20.919 --> 00:52:22.288
and local weather conditions...


00:52:23.855 --> 00:52:25.624
They should be...


00:52:26.259 --> 00:52:28.127
right about...


00:52:29.295 --> 00:52:30.496
here.


00:52:30.629 --> 00:52:33.132
- That's brilliant, sir.
- Thanks...


00:52:33.266 --> 00:52:35.134
for nothing.


00:52:36.969 --> 00:52:39.571
- So, what's on your bucket list?
- Who, me?


00:52:39.704 --> 00:52:41.307
Yeah. Everyone has
a bucket list, right?


00:52:41.441 --> 00:52:42.641
Sure, but...


00:52:42.774 --> 00:52:44.709
I mean, you're the one
leaving Earth, and...


00:52:44.843 --> 00:52:46.446
I'm not planning
on dying anytime soon.


00:52:46.578 --> 00:52:47.879
Don't be so sure.


00:52:48.014 --> 00:52:49.781
Your best friend
is a magnet for danger.


00:52:49.915 --> 00:52:52.051
Are you anointing yourself
as the bestie?


00:52:52.185 --> 00:52:53.319
Mm-hmm.


00:52:53.453 --> 00:52:55.687
A little presumptuous, but...
I mean... What, no...


00:52:55.821 --> 00:52:58.124
I like you, of course, but,


00:52:58.257 --> 00:53:00.059
you know,
we're not best friends.


00:53:00.193 --> 00:53:02.028
You tucked me in last night.


00:53:02.161 --> 00:53:03.795
Fine, fine, fine.
Best animal friend.


00:53:03.930 --> 00:53:05.498
- That would be my dog, Ozzy.
- Okay...


00:53:05.630 --> 00:53:09.302
let's drop this increasingly
humiliating topic of conversation.


00:53:09.435 --> 00:53:11.237
Bucket list.
Give it to me!


00:53:11.803 --> 00:53:13.940
Okay, there is one thing.


00:53:14.673 --> 00:53:16.509
In Green Hills,
I've always felt,


00:53:16.641 --> 00:53:20.012
I don't know, more like a babysitter
than a real cop, you know?


00:53:20.146 --> 00:53:23.015
So I want a chance to prove
myself, under real pressure.


00:53:23.149 --> 00:53:26.285
I'm gonna move to San Francisco,
become a street cop.


00:53:26.419 --> 00:53:29.255
And, I don't know,
see if I have what it takes.


00:53:30.323 --> 00:53:31.357
What?


00:53:32.624 --> 00:53:33.960
Why...
Why is your face doing that?


00:53:34.093 --> 00:53:36.295
You're leaving Green Hills?


00:53:36.761 --> 00:53:37.964
Okay.


00:53:38.097 --> 00:53:40.466
B-B-But why?
Why would you leave Green Hills?


00:53:40.600 --> 00:53:43.269
This may be hard for you to understand,
but Green Hills is a small town.


00:53:43.402 --> 00:53:44.703
It's a very small town.


00:53:44.836 --> 00:53:47.573
Uh, it's not small.
There are hundreds of people.


00:53:47.706 --> 00:53:48.975
That's a small town, dude!


00:53:49.108 --> 00:53:51.910
It's a perfect town,
and the people need you.


00:53:52.044 --> 00:53:53.246
Please.
I clean out their gutters.


00:53:53.379 --> 00:53:55.481
I jump-start their cars
in the winter.


00:53:55.615 --> 00:53:56.848
They could call anybody
to do that.


00:53:56.983 --> 00:53:59.552
Sure, they can call anybody,
but they don't.


00:53:59.684 --> 00:54:01.220
They call you.


00:54:16.602 --> 00:54:20.839
Eeny, meeny, miny...


00:54:21.541 --> 00:54:22.542
mayhem.


00:54:34.153 --> 00:54:35.687
- You're not making any sense.
- Would you calm down?


00:54:35.820 --> 00:54:38.624
You come from a great town with
great people and by my count,


00:54:38.757 --> 00:54:40.927
zero bad guys
trying to kill you!


00:54:43.062 --> 00:54:45.631
Besides, what could possibly
be more important


00:54:45.764 --> 00:54:47.799
than protecting
the people you care about?


00:54:54.073 --> 00:54:56.209
- Look, I get your poi...
- Whoa!


00:54:57.577 --> 00:54:59.011
Yeah!


00:55:06.018 --> 00:55:07.954
You know what?
I was wrong about you.


00:55:08.087 --> 00:55:09.821
You're not
the Donut Lord at all.


00:55:09.956 --> 00:55:11.457
You're more like the Jerk Lord.


00:55:11.591 --> 00:55:14.327
Have you noticed the harpoon
stuck in our dash?


00:55:19.031 --> 00:55:21.067
Sonic!


00:55:21.200 --> 00:55:22.901
I was forced from my home.


00:55:23.035 --> 00:55:25.071
Your home is perfect,
and you're leaving it.


00:55:25.204 --> 00:55:26.905
Why would you do that?


00:55:27.039 --> 00:55:29.642
- Your body!
- Oh, no, not again!


00:55:29.774 --> 00:55:30.742
Hey! Hold on!


00:55:30.875 --> 00:55:32.612
- Why?
- Because I'm gonna do this.


00:55:51.564 --> 00:55:53.032
Sonic!


00:55:53.865 --> 00:55:55.334
Sonic!


00:55:59.472 --> 00:56:02.008
Guess I had a bonus life.


00:56:02.675 --> 00:56:05.678
Oh, yeah, baby!


00:56:05.810 --> 00:56:08.948
Sonic, one. Big Tank, zero.
I'm sorry.


00:56:09.081 --> 00:56:11.450
- Did we get that on camera?
- How are you not dead?


00:56:11.584 --> 00:56:12.817
I have no idea.


00:56:12.952 --> 00:56:15.521
- Do you see me dancing?
- Yes, I saw you dance.


00:56:15.655 --> 00:56:17.189
Is that all you got?


00:56:17.323 --> 00:56:19.258
No, but thank you for asking.


00:56:22.261 --> 00:56:25.498
- Uh-oh.
- Sonic! Get back in the truck!


00:56:25.631 --> 00:56:27.566
You go. I'll catch up.


00:56:31.637 --> 00:56:32.938
Ha!


00:56:38.311 --> 00:56:40.980
I think that tank
just had a baby.


00:56:53.392 --> 00:56:54.460
Incoming!


00:56:56.662 --> 00:56:59.365
- It's my turn!
- You just had one. It's mine!


00:56:59.498 --> 00:57:01.701
Hey, stop fighting
or I'm taking that thing away!


00:57:01.833 --> 00:57:02.802
Yeah, right, Dad.


00:57:14.780 --> 00:57:15.981
Where are you going?


00:57:16.115 --> 00:57:18.417
Just drive the car.
I'll take care of this.


00:57:18.551 --> 00:57:20.553
And if I don't make it,
just ditch me.


00:57:20.686 --> 00:57:22.121
You seem good at that.


00:57:31.664 --> 00:57:33.833
<i>Hey, everyone!
Welcome back to my livestream.</i>


00:57:33.966 --> 00:57:34.934
<i>Today we're destroying robots.</i>


00:57:35.067 --> 00:57:37.036
Step one.


00:57:40.973 --> 00:57:43.242
Yes, we did it!


00:57:47.446 --> 00:57:50.082
We did not do it.
Who <i>is</i> this guy?


00:57:50.216 --> 00:57:52.785
Ever wonder where
your tax dollars are going?


00:57:52.917 --> 00:57:53.953
My turn.


00:57:54.086 --> 00:57:55.588
Here, just keep us
going straight.


00:57:55.721 --> 00:57:56.888
I put it in cruise control.


00:57:57.022 --> 00:57:58.758
I feel just like Vin Diesel.


00:57:58.890 --> 00:58:00.993
"It's all about family, Tom."


00:58:06.999 --> 00:58:08.667
Quick suggestion.


00:58:08.801 --> 00:58:12.138
Roll up into a ball
and smash him with your body.


00:58:13.105 --> 00:58:15.174
Whoa! Where'd you
learn how to drive?


00:58:15.307 --> 00:58:18.077
Here. In this truck.
It's happening as we speak.


00:58:21.180 --> 00:58:23.015
I can't reach it.
Bring him in closer.


00:58:23.149 --> 00:58:24.517
- What?
- Bring it in closer!


00:58:24.650 --> 00:58:26.886
- Hit the brakes.
- Oh, you mean this one?


00:58:27.019 --> 00:58:28.754
The other brakes!


00:58:38.063 --> 00:58:40.366
Ha-ha! Whoo!


00:58:41.367 --> 00:58:43.002
Oh!


00:58:43.135 --> 00:58:46.605
Give me a big, fat break!


00:58:51.677 --> 00:58:54.680
Aw, this one is cute.
Let's keep him.


00:58:55.948 --> 00:58:57.183
Aah!


00:58:57.817 --> 00:58:59.218
Oh, come on!


00:58:59.351 --> 00:59:02.021
How could something
so adorable be so terrible?


00:59:04.957 --> 00:59:06.525
You've got car insurance, right?


00:59:13.165 --> 00:59:14.333
Buzz off.


00:59:14.467 --> 00:59:16.101
That doesn't sound good.


00:59:16.235 --> 00:59:18.437
- No, beeping is bad. Get rid of it!
- I'm trying.


00:59:18.571 --> 00:59:20.306
Throw it out the win...
Throw it anywhere!


00:59:20.439 --> 00:59:23.108
- I can't get it off.
- All right, I'm pulling over.


00:59:30.883 --> 00:59:32.651
- Did I get it?
- Nope.


00:59:33.919 --> 00:59:35.521
Here. Hold still.


00:59:36.489 --> 00:59:38.357
It's going,
it's going...


00:59:38.491 --> 00:59:42.027
It's still here.


00:59:43.195 --> 00:59:44.663
Get off me.


00:59:44.797 --> 00:59:46.499
Ha-ha! Nailed it!


00:59:55.875 --> 00:59:57.376
Sonic!


01:00:04.683 --> 01:00:06.051
No, no, no, no, no.


01:00:12.558 --> 01:00:16.729
Hey. Come on. You're all right.
Wake up. Wake up.


01:00:23.903 --> 01:00:25.604
Did we get 'em?


01:00:25.738 --> 01:00:27.540
Oh. No, there they are.


01:00:27.673 --> 01:00:30.509
They are real survivors,
those two.


01:00:35.414 --> 01:00:37.116
Can we have a moment?


01:00:39.852 --> 01:00:41.320
Pin yourself
to the wall.


01:00:42.588 --> 01:00:44.890
You know, I won't miss you
when you're gone.


01:00:45.025 --> 01:00:47.059
Human beings are
unreliable and stupid,


01:00:47.192 --> 01:00:48.661
and I care very little
about them.


01:00:48.794 --> 01:00:51.697
But my machines are diligent,
relentless.


01:00:51.830 --> 01:00:53.732
They're everything to me!


01:00:55.668 --> 01:00:57.069
Huh?


01:01:16.889 --> 01:01:18.157
Mmm?


01:01:31.403 --> 01:01:32.738
Come on, buddy.


01:01:32.871 --> 01:01:35.608
You're gonna be all right.
You'll be all right.


01:01:40.981 --> 01:01:42.082
- Is Maddie here?
- No, no.


01:01:42.214 --> 01:01:43.415
- Not today. Goodbye.
- It's an emergency!


01:01:43.549 --> 01:01:45.484
- Bye-bye.
- Rachel, stop! Maddie!


01:01:45.618 --> 01:01:47.053
Don't do this.
This is important.


01:01:47.186 --> 01:01:49.221
- Oh, my God! Rachel, let him in.
- I am calling the police.


01:01:49.355 --> 01:01:51.490
No, I am calling the FBI.
I am calling the CIA.


01:01:51.624 --> 01:01:53.392
- Stop. Don't do that.
- I am calling your mother.


01:01:53.525 --> 01:01:55.361
- Okay, got it.
- Maddie, can we talk?


01:01:55.494 --> 01:01:58.297
Tom, what's going on? You're all over
the news. I've been trying to call you.


01:01:58.430 --> 01:02:00.132
I had to ditch my phone
so they couldn't track me.


01:02:00.265 --> 01:02:01.734
- Ditch his phone?
- Track you?


01:02:01.867 --> 01:02:04.136
- Uncle Tommy!
- Jojo! Hey!


01:02:04.269 --> 01:02:06.805
Now your niece is
an accessory to treason.


01:02:06.940 --> 01:02:08.273
- No, she's not.
- Calm down.


01:02:08.407 --> 01:02:10.342
Calm down?
I will not calm down!


01:02:10.476 --> 01:02:12.112
- Enough.
- Yes, calm down. Stop talking.


01:02:12.244 --> 01:02:14.313
No. Ozzy, please.
Good to see you too.


01:02:14.446 --> 01:02:17.216
Oh, little Lord Baby Jesus.


01:02:17.349 --> 01:02:18.550
What is that, Tom?


01:02:18.684 --> 01:02:20.086
Is that plutonium?
Is it e-mails?


01:02:20.219 --> 01:02:21.720
Yes, it's plutonium.


01:02:21.854 --> 01:02:23.789
Can we please go in
the other room and talk...


01:02:23.922 --> 01:02:25.025
Stop it, Ozzy. Quit it!


01:02:25.157 --> 01:02:26.492
This is why I told you
he was no good.


01:02:26.625 --> 01:02:29.062
- I'm not engaging.
- No, Ozzy, quit it.


01:02:31.163 --> 01:02:33.532
Ozzy, no! Ozzy, no!


01:02:34.466 --> 01:02:36.835
Oh, catch me, Jojo.


01:02:36.970 --> 01:02:39.304
Oh, thank God.


01:02:39.438 --> 01:02:42.841
Can I get a glass of water?


01:04:23.709 --> 01:04:25.245
I just thought
you might like a latte


01:04:25.377 --> 01:04:26.946
with steamed Austrian goat milk.


01:04:27.646 --> 01:04:29.515
Who do I look like,
an imbecile?


01:04:29.648 --> 01:04:32.952
Of course I want a latte.
I love the way you make them!


01:04:39.892 --> 01:04:42.095
Ready the prototype.


01:04:42.228 --> 01:04:43.762
With this kind of power,


01:04:43.896 --> 01:04:48.067
my machines can finally reach
their full potential.


01:04:54.439 --> 01:04:56.408
He's gonna be okay, Jojo.


01:04:57.409 --> 01:04:59.979
Oh, thank God.
He's gonna be okay, right?


01:05:00.113 --> 01:05:02.648
I'm a vet, Tom. I don't even
know what I'm looking at here.


01:05:02.781 --> 01:05:05.018
He's a hedgehog.
Or so he says.


01:05:05.151 --> 01:05:06.919
- It talks?
- Almost constantly.


01:05:07.486 --> 01:05:09.655
Okay.


01:05:10.156 --> 01:05:11.323
- Holy...
- What?


01:05:11.456 --> 01:05:12.758
His pulse is super-fast.


01:05:12.891 --> 01:05:14.693
That actually
might be normal for him.


01:05:14.827 --> 01:05:16.461
I don't know.
You gotta help him, Maddie.


01:05:16.595 --> 01:05:18.330
I don't know his physiology.


01:05:18.463 --> 01:05:21.034
He doesn't seem
to have any broken bones.


01:05:21.167 --> 01:05:23.937
He's just really banged up.


01:05:24.770 --> 01:05:27.974
Oh, look at
his poor little feet.


01:05:30.977 --> 01:05:33.846
Hang in there, buddy.
You're gonna be all right.


01:05:36.715 --> 01:05:39.384
Jojo?
Untie your mother. Jojo!


01:05:39.518 --> 01:05:41.720
Untie Mommy.


01:05:41.854 --> 01:05:43.990
Sweetie. Jojo!


01:05:46.993 --> 01:05:48.427
I have to go to the bathroom.


01:05:48.560 --> 01:05:50.596
- He's gonna be okay, right?
- Uh...


01:05:50.729 --> 01:05:53.233
He'll snap out of this.
He'll wake up soon?


01:05:53.365 --> 01:05:54.533
Oh, smelling salts!


01:05:54.666 --> 01:05:55.801
Don't you have, like,
vet smelling salts,


01:05:55.935 --> 01:05:57.769
like for cats or parakeets
or something?


01:05:57.903 --> 01:06:00.739
No. They don't make
cat smelling salts.


01:06:00.873 --> 01:06:03.675
- They should.
- I have human smelling salts


01:06:03.809 --> 01:06:05.878
in my human first aid kit.


01:06:07.180 --> 01:06:08.580
Okay.


01:06:10.350 --> 01:06:11.850
- Here we go.
- Come on, buddy.


01:06:11.985 --> 01:06:13.152
Gotta go fast!


01:06:15.888 --> 01:06:17.656
- Whoa.
- Where am I? What year is it?


01:06:17.789 --> 01:06:19.192
Is The Rock president?


01:06:19.325 --> 01:06:20.525
Whoa, buddy, you're okay.
Calm down.


01:06:20.659 --> 01:06:21.961
Oh, hi, Pretzel Lady!


01:06:22.095 --> 01:06:23.695
Hi.


01:06:24.264 --> 01:06:25.530
- Tom?
- Yeah.


01:06:25.664 --> 01:06:27.033
Can I talk to you, please?


01:06:30.069 --> 01:06:32.338
Space hedgehog, stay there.
Try to rest.


01:06:32.471 --> 01:06:33.872
You got it.
I am great at resting.


01:06:34.007 --> 01:06:36.109
I rest faster than anybody.


01:06:36.242 --> 01:06:37.343
Still talking.


01:06:37.476 --> 01:06:38.877
Uh, first of all,
can we take a moment


01:06:39.012 --> 01:06:40.712
to acknowledge how
under control I've been?


01:06:40.846 --> 01:06:42.547
- Amazing.
- Didn't freak out.


01:06:42.681 --> 01:06:45.084
- No.
- Totally calm.


01:06:45.218 --> 01:06:47.320
- Thank you.
- Ahh.


01:06:47.452 --> 01:06:49.488
Second of all...


01:06:49.621 --> 01:06:52.225
What the heck is going on?
Is that thing an alien?


01:06:52.358 --> 01:06:55.861
Okay, so, remember how Crazy
Carl is always going on


01:06:55.995 --> 01:06:57.696
- about the blue devil?
- The blue devil!


01:06:57.829 --> 01:06:59.865
- That's him? He's real?
- Yeah.


01:06:59.999 --> 01:07:02.101
What is he doing here?
What are you doing here?


01:07:02.235 --> 01:07:04.670
I... kinda sorta...


01:07:04.803 --> 01:07:06.772
shot our little blue friend
with your tranq gun.


01:07:06.905 --> 01:07:09.008
- No, you did not.
- I didn't mean to.


01:07:09.142 --> 01:07:11.044
This is kinda hard
for me to explain.


01:07:11.177 --> 01:07:12.911
And it's gonna sound
a little bit crazy.


01:07:13.046 --> 01:07:15.315
He has to get to
the Transamerica building,


01:07:15.447 --> 01:07:16.882
and I promised
I'd take him.


01:07:17.016 --> 01:07:18.985
Uh-uh! Aliens?


01:07:19.118 --> 01:07:21.586
Maddie, your husband's
lost his mind.


01:07:21.720 --> 01:07:23.655
Use this as an opportunity
to leave him.


01:07:23.789 --> 01:07:25.791
No one would judge you.


01:07:30.495 --> 01:07:32.531
So you won't
hurt your feet anymore.


01:07:33.232 --> 01:07:35.001
- Really?
- Uh-huh.


01:07:35.767 --> 01:07:37.869
No one's ever
given me a gift before.


01:07:38.637 --> 01:07:40.739
I gotta check that
off my bucket list.


01:07:50.450 --> 01:07:52.918
All right! Looking good!


01:07:55.388 --> 01:07:56.822
Okay.


01:07:56.956 --> 01:07:59.292
You said you wanted to help
people in real trouble, right?


01:08:00.026 --> 01:08:01.560
Well, that's what you're doing.


01:08:01.693 --> 01:08:05.131
Blue alien hedgehogs still
count as people. Right?


01:08:05.264 --> 01:08:06.432
- I think so too.
- Yeah.


01:08:06.565 --> 01:08:07.766
- I think.
- Okay.


01:08:07.899 --> 01:08:09.868
I love you.
Did I tell you that already?


01:08:10.003 --> 01:08:12.005
I don't deserve you.
You know that?


01:08:12.138 --> 01:08:13.605
I know that.


01:08:16.042 --> 01:08:18.710
So, you're supposed to be
Tom's best friend


01:08:18.844 --> 01:08:20.346
that he won't shut up about.


01:08:22.281 --> 01:08:23.882
Well, I don't see the appeal.


01:08:25.084 --> 01:08:27.120
Stop!


01:08:27.253 --> 01:08:29.654
That is very gross.


01:08:30.756 --> 01:08:32.125
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:08:32.258 --> 01:08:35.094
So, my truck still runs,
but it's pretty much totaled.


01:08:35.228 --> 01:08:37.363
You think your sister would
mind if we borrowed her car?


01:08:37.497 --> 01:08:39.198
You have got to be kidding me!


01:08:40.199 --> 01:08:41.566
- She'll be fine.
- Yeah, let's do that.


01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:43.069
Mm-hmm.


01:08:43.202 --> 01:08:45.371
This is my house!


01:08:45.505 --> 01:08:47.340
Coming through!


01:08:47.473 --> 01:08:50.609
Whoa, whoa! Now this is my turn,
and I go around you.


01:08:50.742 --> 01:08:52.577
Sorry! And...


01:08:52.711 --> 01:08:54.913
- perfect park.
- What are you, crazy?


01:08:55.048 --> 01:08:56.215
Is there anything
you didn't hit?


01:08:56.349 --> 01:08:57.849
Why did we let the alien drive?


01:08:57.984 --> 01:09:01.187
Hey, I got us here.
And please, five stars.


01:09:02.687 --> 01:09:05.924
- So, this is it?
- That's it. That's your pyramid.


01:09:06.059 --> 01:09:08.261
Wow, look at that thing!


01:09:08.394 --> 01:09:09.728
What happens now?


01:09:10.430 --> 01:09:13.166
- Oh. He's... gone.
- Yep.


01:09:14.200 --> 01:09:16.936
No good. You need a special
key to get to the roof.


01:09:18.171 --> 01:09:19.571
What now?


01:09:19.704 --> 01:09:22.774
Time for me to abuse
the power entrusted to me.


01:09:32.518 --> 01:09:34.719
We got a jumper on the roof.
Gotta get up there fast


01:09:34.853 --> 01:09:37.123
or we're gonna have
a human pancake on our hands.


01:09:37.256 --> 01:09:39.325
You came all the way
from Montana.


01:09:40.460 --> 01:09:42.195
Yeah. That's how serious it is.


01:09:47.066 --> 01:09:48.101
Okay.


01:09:49.768 --> 01:09:51.270
You just saved a life.


01:09:59.946 --> 01:10:02.848
How much longer?
I can't breathe in here.


01:10:04.749 --> 01:10:07.053
Hello?
Anybody there?


01:10:07.186 --> 01:10:09.455
Do you have your child
in that bag?


01:10:09.589 --> 01:10:10.789
No.


01:10:10.922 --> 01:10:13.392
I mean, yes, it's a child,
but it's not mine.


01:10:14.460 --> 01:10:15.394
It's not your child.


01:10:15.528 --> 01:10:17.863
Relax.
I'm a cop, okay?


01:10:17.997 --> 01:10:19.499
Plus, he likes it in there,
don't you, buddy?


01:10:19.631 --> 01:10:21.000
Why would I
like it in here?


01:10:21.134 --> 01:10:24.203
This is worse than the dog cage
you had me in earlier.


01:10:25.071 --> 01:10:27.839
Such a kidder.


01:10:27.974 --> 01:10:30.709
- Okay.
- No, I'm scared of the dark!


01:10:31.210 --> 01:10:32.711
Is anybody there?


01:10:44.223 --> 01:10:47.493
What were you
keeping in this bag?


01:10:47.627 --> 01:10:48.995
A jar of pickled farts?


01:10:49.128 --> 01:10:50.963
All right.
What are we looking for?


01:10:53.933 --> 01:10:55.667
This.


01:10:56.402 --> 01:10:58.037
Okay.
What happens now?


01:10:58.171 --> 01:10:59.972
Now all I have to do
is think of where I want


01:11:00.106 --> 01:11:02.341
the other end of the ring
to appear, and I throw it.


01:11:02.475 --> 01:11:04.443
So that's it?
We did it?


01:11:04.577 --> 01:11:06.312
Yeah. We did it!


01:11:06.445 --> 01:11:10.016
Hey. Sorry we didn't get to do
everything on your bucket list, pal.


01:11:10.149 --> 01:11:12.884
It's okay.
I did the ones I needed the most.


01:11:13.019 --> 01:11:16.422
You two are so cute.


01:11:16.556 --> 01:11:18.690
- Oh, please. What?
- We are not.


01:11:18.823 --> 01:11:20.326
No.
We're not cute.


01:11:20.459 --> 01:11:23.029
We are a couple of loose cannons
just living by our own rules.


01:11:23.162 --> 01:11:23.895
Exactly.


01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:25.364
- Really?
- Yeah.


01:11:25.498 --> 01:11:28.134
And our rules include
expressing heartfelt emotions.


01:11:28.267 --> 01:11:29.535
If you say so.


01:11:29.669 --> 01:11:32.238
- Okay, then.
- All right.


01:11:33.172 --> 01:11:35.041
- Um, you gotta go, right?
- Yeah, I gotta go.


01:11:35.174 --> 01:11:36.509
I gotta go.
We gotta go too.


01:11:36.642 --> 01:11:38.344
See... All right, bye-bye.


01:11:42.881 --> 01:11:44.951
Just one more thing.


01:11:52.625 --> 01:11:54.927
I'm sorry I was so hard on you.


01:11:57.330 --> 01:12:00.333
I know it's a tough decision
for you to leave Green Hills.


01:12:00.466 --> 01:12:03.236
Walking away from
something you care about


01:12:03.868 --> 01:12:05.071
has to be painful.


01:12:05.204 --> 01:12:07.340
You're not sure
you really want to go, huh?


01:12:08.374 --> 01:12:11.743
I don't want to go,
but I can't stay.


01:12:11.876 --> 01:12:14.513
As long as I'm here,
I put everyone in danger.


01:12:14.981 --> 01:12:17.149
I can't do that.


01:12:17.283 --> 01:12:21.487
I just want you to know that
these last two days have been


01:12:21.621 --> 01:12:24.290
the best two days of my life.


01:12:27.260 --> 01:12:28.694
You know, I never
thought I'd say this,


01:12:28.827 --> 01:12:31.530
but I'm actually gonna miss
you, you little blue devil.


01:12:31.664 --> 01:12:33.466
I'll miss you too,
Donut Lord.


01:12:34.467 --> 01:12:35.501
Thank you.


01:12:36.202 --> 01:12:37.236
For what?


01:12:38.004 --> 01:12:39.804
For saving my life.


01:12:57.423 --> 01:13:00.493
Okay. Did someone leave
their "Find My Phone" on?


01:13:27.086 --> 01:13:30.022
Welcome to San Francisco,
Mr. Wachowski.


01:13:30.855 --> 01:13:32.425
Are you enjoying
the clam chowder?


01:13:32.558 --> 01:13:34.826
It's the government wack job
who keeps trying to kill us.


01:13:34.960 --> 01:13:36.262
Unsuccessfully!


01:13:36.395 --> 01:13:38.230
Nice of you to swing by
on your way to Comic-Con.


01:13:38.364 --> 01:13:40.433
Yeah,
what are you wearing?


01:13:41.866 --> 01:13:43.336
It's a flight suit,


01:13:43.469 --> 01:13:46.072
designed to modulate my body
temperature and reduce drag.


01:13:46.205 --> 01:13:47.807
Yeah, and yet
you still are one.


01:13:47.940 --> 01:13:49.709
Ooh-hoo! Good one.


01:13:49.841 --> 01:13:51.544
You are catching fire,
Thomas.


01:13:51.677 --> 01:13:54.680
Oh, and speaking of heat,
I see you've taken a lover.


01:13:54.814 --> 01:13:56.048
Does she have a name


01:13:56.182 --> 01:13:58.484
or should we just call her
"collateral damage"?


01:13:58.617 --> 01:14:00.086
Hey, watch your mouth.


01:14:00.219 --> 01:14:02.021
Unless you want a little more
of what I gave you earlier?


01:14:02.154 --> 01:14:03.556
I punched him
in the face.


01:14:03.689 --> 01:14:05.725
Oh! He punched him right in the face!
It was awesome!


01:14:05.857 --> 01:14:08.928
The time for talking is over!
It's time to push buttons.


01:14:09.061 --> 01:14:12.131
Your flying eggs are pretty
impressive, Mr. Eggman,


01:14:12.264 --> 01:14:14.633
but let's face it,
you'll never catch me.


01:14:14.767 --> 01:14:16.402
Confidence!


01:14:16.535 --> 01:14:19.004
A fool's substitute
for intelligence.


01:14:26.679 --> 01:14:28.447
- That's not good.
- Uh...


01:14:28.581 --> 01:14:30.483
Sonic, I know you got the
super-speed and everything,


01:14:30.616 --> 01:14:33.719
- but Maddie and I...
- Totally defenseless? Probably gonna get blown up?


01:14:33.853 --> 01:14:35.755
Pretty much, yeah.


01:14:35.887 --> 01:14:38.591
Don't worry.
I know exactly what to do.


01:14:45.998 --> 01:14:47.833
I was not expecting that.


01:14:47.967 --> 01:14:51.170
But I was expecting not to expect
something, so it doesn't count.


01:15:33.546 --> 01:15:35.514
Pew, pew-pew-pew,
pew-pew-pew-pew!


01:15:39.351 --> 01:15:42.455
Oh!


01:15:51.063 --> 01:15:52.531
Come on!


01:15:53.098 --> 01:15:54.733
Come on, come on, come on.


01:16:06.879 --> 01:16:09.348
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
No, no, no!


01:16:21.193 --> 01:16:22.862
Oh! Hi, Tom.


01:16:22.995 --> 01:16:25.097
Glad you're here.
Could use some help.


01:16:25.231 --> 01:16:26.967
Old Bessie's about to give birth.


01:16:27.099 --> 01:16:29.368
Give me a minute.


01:16:29.869 --> 01:16:31.170
Aah.


01:16:32.204 --> 01:16:35.608
Can I give you one
genius piece of advice?


01:16:35.976 --> 01:16:37.409
Don't run.


01:16:37.543 --> 01:16:39.745
It'll only hurt more if you do.


01:16:39.879 --> 01:16:42.248
And it's bad for your joints.
They've proved it.


01:16:42.381 --> 01:16:44.783
All right, Eggman.
You wanna get fast?


01:16:44.917 --> 01:16:45.986
Let's get fast.


01:16:49.255 --> 01:16:50.689
The hard way it is.


01:17:09.742 --> 01:17:11.744
That was an illegal left,
by the way.


01:17:14.380 --> 01:17:16.282
<i>So, here we are again.</i>


01:17:16.415 --> 01:17:17.917
<i>We've been through
so much together.</i>


01:17:18.050 --> 01:17:20.686
<i>Now you understand why there's
a psychotic robot doctor</i>


01:17:20.819 --> 01:17:23.122
<i>chasing a supersonic
blue hedgehog.</i>


01:17:23.255 --> 01:17:26.158
<i>Want to know how it ends?
Yeah, me too.</i>


01:17:43.709 --> 01:17:44.643
How is this possible?


01:17:44.777 --> 01:17:47.279
No one's ever
caught up to me before.


01:17:54.887 --> 01:17:56.689
Coming through!


01:17:56.822 --> 01:17:57.856
<i>Sacrebleu!</i>


01:17:58.724 --> 01:18:01.293
<i>Excusez-moi, monsieur!</i>


01:18:05.031 --> 01:18:07.466
Here we go.
Room to open it up.


01:18:16.442 --> 01:18:17.876
I can't lose him!


01:18:32.092 --> 01:18:34.893
If you can't beat 'em,
blind 'em.


01:18:37.964 --> 01:18:40.232
Lost visual contact.


01:18:44.837 --> 01:18:48.807
You're not allowed up there!
It's one of the Seven Wonders!


01:19:13.033 --> 01:19:14.700
Get out of here!


01:19:22.408 --> 01:19:25.844
You're an astonishing
little creature.


01:19:27.813 --> 01:19:29.949
It'll be fun to take you
back to the lab


01:19:30.083 --> 01:19:32.718
for a litany of invasive
exploratory procedures.


01:19:33.485 --> 01:19:35.421
Any last words?


01:19:36.156 --> 01:19:39.191
Guac. I like that word.


01:19:40.592 --> 01:19:42.695
I don't have to tell you how
many scientific breakthroughs


01:19:42.828 --> 01:19:45.264
have been made possible
by animal testing.


01:19:45.397 --> 01:19:46.598
You're being very selfish.


01:19:46.732 --> 01:19:47.800
Going my way?


01:19:47.934 --> 01:19:49.035
What the...


01:19:54.440 --> 01:19:56.608
Who the hell
do you think you are?


01:19:59.678 --> 01:20:01.213
I'm the Donut Lord,
you son of a...


01:20:06.385 --> 01:20:08.387
Autopilot, adjust.


01:20:08.955 --> 01:20:10.255
Why?


01:20:10.389 --> 01:20:13.525
Why would you throw
your life away for this thing?


01:20:13.659 --> 01:20:14.928
That's why I don't have friends.


01:20:15.061 --> 01:20:17.229
Next thing you know,
you're somebody's best man.


01:20:17.362 --> 01:20:18.697
They want to have
the wedding out of town.


01:20:18.831 --> 01:20:21.101
Like nobody has anything
better to do!


01:20:21.734 --> 01:20:23.702
Anyway, where were we?


01:20:23.836 --> 01:20:26.672
Oh, yes.
You were about to die.


01:20:28.674 --> 01:20:30.676
That's our sheriff
you're messing with.


01:20:32.212 --> 01:20:33.947
And our blue devil...


01:20:34.080 --> 01:20:37.382
who as everyone can see
is a very real creature,


01:20:37.516 --> 01:20:40.285
and not at all invented by me.


01:20:42.588 --> 01:20:44.523
- Oh, careful.
- Just... Just put it away.


01:20:44.656 --> 01:20:45.858
Tom?


01:20:59.371 --> 01:21:01.040
I don't mean
to be indelicate here,


01:21:01.174 --> 01:21:04.944
but someone should get some ice,
keep the body fresh.


01:21:07.713 --> 01:21:10.150
He's just a silly little alien.


01:21:10.649 --> 01:21:12.284
He didn't belong here!


01:21:14.220 --> 01:21:16.388
That little alien


01:21:16.522 --> 01:21:19.959
knew more about being human
than you ever will.


01:21:20.492 --> 01:21:21.827
His name was Sonic.


01:21:22.895 --> 01:21:24.296
This was his home.


01:21:25.198 --> 01:21:26.698
And he was my friend.


01:21:51.890 --> 01:21:53.026
He's all yours.


01:21:54.593 --> 01:21:55.962
Everyone, get back!


01:21:59.531 --> 01:22:02.501
I think you have something
that belongs to me.


01:22:03.102 --> 01:22:04.336
Whoa.


01:22:13.279 --> 01:22:14.913
This is my power.


01:22:15.048 --> 01:22:17.649
And I'm not using it
to run away anymore.


01:22:17.783 --> 01:22:21.587
I'm using it
to protect my friends.


01:23:18.610 --> 01:23:20.646
Ooh! Now you've done it!


01:23:20.779 --> 01:23:22.148
Guess what, Eggman?


01:23:22.282 --> 01:23:24.951
I'm not leaving Earth. You are.


01:23:25.417 --> 01:23:26.885
Donut Lord?


01:24:15.734 --> 01:24:18.204
- I told you, you got this.
- Hey, <i>we</i> got this.


01:24:30.950 --> 01:24:33.152
- I think these belong to you.
- Thank you very much.


01:24:34.586 --> 01:24:36.189
No more pushing people
off of buildings.


01:24:36.322 --> 01:24:37.957
You know
I can't promise that.


01:24:41.394 --> 01:24:44.130
- You did pretty good, space hog.
- Thanks, Donut Lord.


01:24:44.263 --> 01:24:47.300
You're gonna have to explain
this "Donut Lord" thing.


01:24:47.433 --> 01:24:50.236
Nope, sorry. That's for me
and the little guy. Right?


01:24:50.370 --> 01:24:53.772
- We got our thing, you got your thing with your... sister.
- Oh, my God, my sister.


01:24:53.905 --> 01:24:58.610
Gotta go fast. Gotta go fast.
Gotta go fast. Gotta go fast.


01:24:58.744 --> 01:25:00.679
Jojo, put on my Fitbit...


01:25:01.513 --> 01:25:03.182
so I can at least
get some steps.


01:25:03.316 --> 01:25:04.816
We can never go back there.


01:25:06.219 --> 01:25:07.753
I mean, are we?


01:25:09.688 --> 01:25:12.557
'Cause it kind of feels like
we're home right now.


01:25:12.691 --> 01:25:13.960
Really?


01:25:15.294 --> 01:25:18.498
I kind of feel like
I checked the "save a life" box


01:25:18.630 --> 01:25:20.033
off my bucket list.


01:25:22.468 --> 01:25:24.603
Now all I want to do
is spend my life


01:25:24.736 --> 01:25:26.571
with the people
I care about.


01:25:27.672 --> 01:25:29.108
I want to check that box.


01:25:30.343 --> 01:25:32.544
Okay, I like that.


01:25:32.677 --> 01:25:35.181
All right, everybody.
Nothing to see here.


01:25:35.314 --> 01:25:36.482
Let's disperse.


01:25:36.615 --> 01:25:38.284
Just another ordinary day
in Green Hills.


01:25:38.418 --> 01:25:40.019
Carl,
I'll take that chain saw.


01:25:40.619 --> 01:25:42.155
Come on. Let's go!


01:25:42.288 --> 01:25:44.157
You act like
you've never seen a fight


01:25:44.290 --> 01:25:48.894
between an intergalactic space
rodent and a robot with a doctorate.


01:25:57.803 --> 01:25:59.571
You got enough there?


01:25:59.704 --> 01:26:01.640
- Yes, Mr. Manager.
- Need any more?


01:26:01.773 --> 01:26:03.342
You get that away.


01:26:13.819 --> 01:26:15.587
Mr. and Mrs. Wachowski?


01:26:16.522 --> 01:26:17.756
Yes?


01:26:19.791 --> 01:26:21.561
A token of appreciation
from your government,


01:26:21.693 --> 01:26:25.164
for keeping quiet about recent
incidents, which never occurred.


01:26:27.533 --> 01:26:29.035
Wow!


01:26:29.168 --> 01:26:31.803
- Wonder what it is.
- Money to fix the house?


01:26:31.938 --> 01:26:34.273
- Letter from the President?
- You'll see.


01:26:34.407 --> 01:26:35.975
Okay.


01:26:38.844 --> 01:26:40.846
- Olive Garden.
- Hmm, yeah.


01:26:40.980 --> 01:26:43.282
The way you said
"You'll see" made me think


01:26:43.416 --> 01:26:45.218
it was something better
than the things we said.


01:26:45.351 --> 01:26:48.121
Have you tried their
Never Ending Pasta Bowl?


01:26:48.254 --> 01:26:49.721
It never ends.


01:26:49.855 --> 01:26:52.024
- That sounds... fancy.
- Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.


01:26:52.158 --> 01:26:55.328
Well, thank you.
We appreciate the gesture.


01:26:55.461 --> 01:26:58.464
Oh, hey. I guess we can close the
file on that Robotnik guy, huh?


01:26:58.598 --> 01:26:59.532
Just disappeared.


01:26:59.664 --> 01:27:00.899
I'm sorry,


01:27:01.033 --> 01:27:04.337
but no such person exists
or ever has existed.


01:27:05.670 --> 01:27:06.838
I wish that were true.


01:27:06.973 --> 01:27:08.441
You haven't by any chance
been in contact


01:27:08.574 --> 01:27:11.177
with a certain alien creature
since the incident, have you?


01:27:11.310 --> 01:27:13.012
Uncle Sam would love
to have a chat with him.


01:27:13.146 --> 01:27:15.914
Very casual.
Brunch, perhaps.


01:27:17.517 --> 01:27:18.551
Oh, you mean
the little blue guy.


01:27:18.683 --> 01:27:19.619
- Mmm.
- No.


01:27:19.751 --> 01:27:21.686
- No, nothing. No.
- Mm-mmm.


01:27:21.820 --> 01:27:24.190
- Doubt we'll ever hear from him again.
- Mm-mmm.


01:27:24.723 --> 01:27:26.259
Very well.


01:27:26.691 --> 01:27:28.161
Okay.


01:27:28.294 --> 01:27:29.861
- Thank you.
- Great.


01:27:29.996 --> 01:27:31.097
Mmm.


01:27:32.031 --> 01:27:32.764
Yep.


01:27:36.269 --> 01:27:38.504
To be honest, I'm pretty
pumped about the pasta bowl.


01:27:39.972 --> 01:27:41.574
So, do you guys wanna
watch a movie or what?


01:27:41.706 --> 01:27:42.874
Sorry, buddy,
it's a school night.


01:27:43.009 --> 01:27:44.510
It's time for you
to go back to your cave.


01:27:44.644 --> 01:27:46.678
What?
It's 3:00 in the afternoon!


01:27:46.811 --> 01:27:48.414
You know how you get
when you're tired. Come on.


01:27:48.548 --> 01:27:49.881
Me? I'm not like anything.


01:27:50.016 --> 01:27:53.119
- You guys are so uncool.
- Yeah, yeah, we know.


01:27:53.252 --> 01:27:55.087
Hey, buddy, where you going?


01:27:55.221 --> 01:27:56.956
You said I have to
go back to my cave.


01:27:57.557 --> 01:27:58.924
We did.


01:28:13.606 --> 01:28:16.209
Oh, my... Are you kidding me?


01:28:17.610 --> 01:28:19.312
I can't believe it.


01:28:19.445 --> 01:28:20.879
How did you...


01:28:21.581 --> 01:28:23.848
It's... It's all here.


01:28:33.926 --> 01:28:36.162
Look at this! Are you kidding?
And the beanbag?


01:28:36.295 --> 01:28:38.231
No way!
How did you even get this?


01:28:38.364 --> 01:28:41.000
And you got it all the way over...
Oh!


01:28:41.133 --> 01:28:43.236
I love it, I love it,
I love it, I love it!


01:28:45.904 --> 01:28:49.408
Well, welcome home.


01:28:49.542 --> 01:28:52.211
Thank you, so much.


01:29:01.087 --> 01:29:02.355
<i>Oh, no, you don't.</i>


01:29:02.488 --> 01:29:05.224
<i>No second-best animal friends
allowed in my room.</i>


01:29:05.358 --> 01:29:07.026
<i>Wait. What are you doing?</i>


01:29:07.159 --> 01:29:09.362
<i>Stay away from me.
Stop it!</i>


01:29:09.495 --> 01:29:11.631
<i>I'm warning you.
I've got nunchucks!</i>


01:29:11.763 --> 01:29:14.100
<i>Hey, stop.
Okay, you can stay.</i>


01:29:31.317 --> 01:29:35.154
My grasp on sanity remains...
absolute.


01:29:36.722 --> 01:29:38.424
Isn't that right,
Agent Stone?


01:29:43.329 --> 01:29:45.564
Why don't you get a head start?


01:29:47.500 --> 01:29:50.436
Do some rock-connaissance.


01:29:50.569 --> 01:29:53.639
Rock-connaissance!
Come on! That's hilarious!


01:29:53.773 --> 01:29:55.308
What's the matter with you?


01:29:55.441 --> 01:29:59.045
Here's the "sitch." Uninhabited planet.


01:30:00.279 --> 01:30:04.483
No resources, no supplies,
no apparent way home.


01:30:06.885 --> 01:30:08.587
A lesser man would die here.


01:30:11.791 --> 01:30:13.559
I'll be home by Christmas.


01:30:33.045 --> 01:30:35.181
Rock-connaissance!


01:30:38.117 --> 01:30:40.386
Come on! Cheer up!


01:32:42.074 --> 01:32:44.577
If these readings are accurate,
he's here.


01:32:44.710 --> 01:32:45.878
I found him.


01:32:46.011 --> 01:32:48.080
I just hope I'm not too late.


01:33:02.393 --> 01:33:07.393
